window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-06-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3"]={"id":"CGL-06-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3","title":"CGL 06 OCT 2026 SHIFT 3","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000074081","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"<b>Address A</b>: 5<sup>th</sup> Cross, 10<sup>th</sup> Main, Indiranagar, Chennai – 600020<br><b>Address B</b>: 10<sup>th</sup> Cross, 5<sup>th</sup> Main, Indiranagar, Chennai – 600020<br>Are these addresses likely to be the same? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>पता A</b>: 5<sup>th</sup> Cross, 10<sup>th</sup> Main, Indiranagar, Chennai – 600020<br><b>पता B</b>: 10<sup>th</sup> Cross, 5<sup>th</sup> Main, Indiranagar, Chennai – 600020<br>क्या ये दोनों पते एक ही होने की संभावना है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Yes","hi":"हाँ"},"2":{"en":"No, city differs","hi":"नहीं, शहर अलग है"},"3":{"en":"No, cross and main street differs","hi":"नहीं, क्रॉस और मेन स्ट्रीट अलग है"},"4":{"en":"No, pin code differs","hi":"नहीं, पिन कोड अलग है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Compare the two addresses part by part.<br>Indiranagar, Chennai and the PIN 600020 are the same in both.<br>In Address A the house is on the <b>5<sup>th</sup> Cross</b> with the <b>10<sup>th</sup> Main</b>, while in Address B it is on the <b>10<sup>th</sup> Cross</b> with the <b>5<sup>th</sup> Main</b> — the cross and the main road are interchanged.<br>A cross street and a main road are two different streets, so the two addresses show two different locations.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): No, cross and main street differs.</b>","hi":"दोनों पतों की भाग-दर-भाग तुलना कीजिए।<br>Indiranagar, Chennai तथा पिन कोड 600020 दोनों में समान हैं।<br>पता A में मकान <b>5<sup>th</sup> Cross</b> तथा <b>10<sup>th</sup> Main</b> पर है, जबकि पता B में वह <b>10<sup>th</sup> Cross</b> तथा <b>5<sup>th</sup> Main</b> पर है — अर्थात् क्रॉस और मेन स्ट्रीट आपस में बदल गए हैं।<br>क्रॉस स्ट्रीट और मेन रोड दो भिन्न सड़कें हैं, इसलिए दोनों पते दो अलग स्थानों को दर्शाते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): नहीं, क्रॉस और मेन स्ट्रीट अलग है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000074082","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"STONE\" is written as \"RSNMD.\" How will \"CHAIR\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"STONE\" को \"RSNMD.\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"CHAIR\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BGBHQ"},"2":{"en":"BGZHO"},"3":{"en":"BGZHQ"},"4":{"en":"BGBHO"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"STONE → RSNMD<br>S − 1 = R, T − 1 = S, O − 1 = N, N − 1 = M, E − 1 = D<br>Each letter moves one step backward.<br>CHAIR: C − 1 = B, H − 1 = G, A − 1 = Z, I − 1 = H, R − 1 = Q<br>Code = <b>BGZHQ</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): BGZHQ.</b>","hi":"STONE → RSNMD<br>S − 1 = R, T − 1 = S, O − 1 = N, N − 1 = M, E − 1 = D<br>प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान पीछे खिसकता है।<br>CHAIR: C − 1 = B, H − 1 = G, A − 1 = Z, I − 1 = H, R − 1 = Q<br>कूट = <b>BGZHQ</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): BGZHQ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000074083","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"COMMUNICATION\" is written as \"DONMVNJCBTJOO\". How will \"EDUCATIONALLY\" be written? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"COMMUNICATION\" को \"DONMVNJCBTJOO\" लिखा जाता है। \"EDUCATIONALLY\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"FDVCBTJOOAMLZ"},"2":{"en":"FDCBTJOOAMLZ"},"3":{"en":"FDVCBTJOAOMLZ"},"4":{"en":"FDVCBTOIOAMLZ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"COMMUNICATION → DONMVNJCBTJOO<br>Letters at odd places move one step forward (C → D, M → N, U → V, I → J, A → B, I → J, N → O) and letters at even places stay unchanged (O, M, N, C, T, O).<br>EDUCATIONALLY: odd places E, U, A, I, N, L, Y → F, V, B, J, O, M, Z; even places D, C, T, O, A, L stay as they are.<br>Code = <b>FDVCBTJOOAMLZ</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): FDVCBTJOOAMLZ.</b>","hi":"COMMUNICATION → DONMVNJCBTJOO<br>विषम स्थानों के अक्षर एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं (C → D, M → N, U → V, I → J, A → B, I → J, N → O) तथा सम स्थानों के अक्षर अपरिवर्तित रहते हैं (O, M, N, C, T, O)।<br>EDUCATIONALLY: विषम स्थान E, U, A, I, N, L, Y → F, V, B, J, O, M, Z; सम स्थान D, C, T, O, A, L जैसे हैं वैसे ही रहते हैं।<br>कूट = <b>FDVCBTJOOAMLZ</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): FDVCBTJOOAMLZ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000074084","section":"REASONING","topic":"Order & Ranking","question":{"en":"In a row of players, Mohan is 6<sup>th</sup> from the left, and Sohan is 20<sup>th</sup> from the right. After swapping their places, Mohan becomes 18<sup>th</sup> from the left. Find the total number of players. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"खिलाड़ियों की एक पंक्ति में मोहन बाएँ से 6<sup>वें</sup> स्थान पर है और सोहन दाएँ से 20<sup>वें</sup> स्थान पर है। अपने स्थान बदलने के बाद मोहन बाएँ से 18<sup>वें</sup> हो जाता है। खिलाड़ियों की कुल संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"33"},"2":{"en":"35"},"3":{"en":"37"},"4":{"en":"39"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"After the swap Mohan stands at Sohan's place, and that place is 18<sup>th</sup> from the left.<br>So Sohan's original place is 18<sup>th</sup> from the left and 20<sup>th</sup> from the right.<br>Total = 18 + 20 − 1 = 37<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 37.</b>","hi":"स्थान बदलने के बाद मोहन सोहन के स्थान पर पहुँच जाता है, जो बाएँ से 18<sup>वाँ</sup> है।<br>अतः सोहन का मूल स्थान बाएँ से 18<sup>वाँ</sup> तथा दाएँ से 20<sup>वाँ</sup> है।<br>कुल = 18 + 20 − 1 = 37<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 37 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000074085","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A newly appointed department head reports to a senior director who is highly anxious about an upcoming internal audit and tends to micro-manage minor tasks, affecting team efficiency. How should the department head apply empathy and adaptive leadership to handle this situation effectively? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक नवनियुक्त विभागाध्यक्ष एक वरिष्ठ निदेशक के अधीन कार्य करता है, जो आगामी आंतरिक लेखा-परीक्षा को लेकर अत्यधिक चिंतित रहते हैं और छोटे-छोटे कार्यों में भी अनावश्यक हस्तक्षेप करते हैं, जिससे टीम की कार्यक्षमता प्रभावित हो रही है। इस स्थिति को प्रभावी ढंग से संभालने के लिए विभागाध्यक्ष को सहानुभूति तथा अनुकूलनशील नेतृत्व का प्रयोग कैसे करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ignore the director's micro-management tactics and instruct the team to follow only the head's direct commands.","hi":"निदेशक की अत्यधिक हस्तक्षेप की रणनीति को अनदेखा करें और टीम को केवल विभागाध्यक्ष के सीधे आदेश मानने का निर्देश दें।"},"2":{"en":"File a formal complaint with higher management requesting the senior director's transfer due to interference.","hi":"हस्तक्षेप के कारण वरिष्ठ निदेशक के स्थानांतरण का अनुरोध करते हुए उच्च प्रबंधन के पास औपचारिक शिकायत दर्ज करें।"},"3":{"en":"Match the director's anxiety by introducing stricter daily monitoring systems for all staff members.","hi":"निदेशक की चिंता के अनुरूप सभी कर्मचारियों के लिए और कठोर दैनिक अनुश्रवण प्रणाली शुरू करें।"},"4":{"en":"Schedule a private meeting to provide structured audit updates and ease the director's underlying anxiety.","hi":"व्यक्तिगत बैठक का समय निर्धारित करें, जिसमें लेखा-परीक्षा की सुव्यवस्थित जानकारी दें और निदेशक की मूल चिंता को कम करें।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The director's interference comes from anxiety about the audit, not from distrust of the team.<br>Since the head cannot stop the audit, the useful response is to reduce the director's uncertainty with regular, structured updates given in a private meeting.<br>Ignoring the director, complaining for a transfer or copying the anxiety with stricter monitoring only increases friction and lowers efficiency.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Schedule a private meeting to provide structured audit updates and ease the director's underlying anxiety.</b>","hi":"निदेशक का हस्तक्षेप लेखा-परीक्षा की चिंता के कारण है, टीम पर अविश्वास के कारण नहीं।<br>लेखा-परीक्षा रुक नहीं सकती, इसलिए उपयुक्त उपाय यह है कि व्यक्तिगत बैठक में नियमित और सुव्यवस्थित जानकारी देकर निदेशक की अनिश्चितता कम की जाए।<br>निदेशक को अनदेखा करना, स्थानांतरण की शिकायत करना या उसी चिंता के साथ कठोर अनुश्रवण बढ़ाना केवल टकराव और कार्यक्षमता में कमी लाएगा।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): व्यक्तिगत बैठक का समय निर्धारित करें, जिसमें लेखा-परीक्षा की सुव्यवस्थित जानकारी दें और निदेशक की मूल चिंता को कम करें।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000074086","section":"REASONING","topic":"Counting Figures","question":{"en":"How many triangles are there in the given figure?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019e8e4a-72cf-7d3c-8a60-3076f202e08d_EN.jpg?edu=639294371617599418\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई आकृति में कितने त्रिभुज हैं?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019e8e4a-72cf-7d3c-8a60-3076f202e08d_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739542672\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9"},"2":{"en":"11"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"13"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Count the triangles size-wise.<br>Smallest (single part) triangles = 6<br>Triangles made of two parts = 4<br>Triangles made of three parts = 2<br>Largest triangle = 1<br>Total = 6 + 4 + 2 + 1 = 13<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 13.</b>","hi":"त्रिभुजों को आकार के अनुसार गिनिए।<br>सबसे छोटे (एक भाग के) त्रिभुज = 6<br>दो भागों से बने त्रिभुज = 4<br>तीन भागों से बने त्रिभुज = 2<br>सबसे बड़ा त्रिभुज = 1<br>कुल = 6 + 4 + 2 + 1 = 13<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 13 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019e8e4a-72cf-7d3c-8a60-3076f202e08d_EN.jpg?edu=639294371617599418","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019e8e4a-72cf-7d3c-8a60-3076f202e08d_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739542672"]}},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000074087","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During a meeting, a junior colleague proposes an idea that lacks clear articulation but holds significant potential, only to be quickly dismissed by the manager. Observing the employee's visible discouragement, what is the most professional and constructive action you should take? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बैठक में एक कनिष्ठ सहकर्मी ऐसा विचार रखता है, जिसकी प्रस्तुति स्पष्ट नहीं है, परंतु उसमें काफी संभावना है, और प्रबंधक उसे तुरंत खारिज कर देते हैं। कर्मचारी की स्पष्ट निराशा देखकर आपको सबसे व्यावसायिक और रचनात्मक कार्रवाई क्या करनी चाहिए? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Remain entirely silent because challenging the manager's decision in the moment might be unwise.","hi":"पूरी तरह चुप रहें, क्योंकि उस क्षण प्रबंधक के निर्णय को चुनौती देना उचित नहीं हो सकता।"},"2":{"en":"Arrange to meet the employee later to tell them that they really need to speak more clearly.","hi":"बाद में कर्मचारी से मिलकर बताएँ कि उन्हें और स्पष्ट बोलने की आवश्यकता है।"},"3":{"en":"Make a lighthearted joke about the situation in order to help lighten the overall team mood.","hi":"स्थिति पर हल्का-फुल्का मजाक करें ताकि पूरी टीम का माहौल हल्का हो जाए।"},"4":{"en":"Reframe their idea using better terminology during the meeting and suggest revisiting the proposal.","hi":"बैठक के दौरान बेहतर शब्दावली में उनके विचार को फिर से प्रस्तुत करें तथा प्रस्ताव पर पुनर्विचार का सुझाव दें।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The idea has merit; only its presentation was weak.<br>Restating the idea clearly in the meeting keeps the value of the suggestion alive and protects the junior colleague's confidence, while still respecting the manager's authority.<br>Silence, a lecture later, or a joke do not save the idea.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Reframe their idea using better terminology during the meeting and suggest revisiting the proposal.</b>","hi":"विचार में गुण है; कमी केवल प्रस्तुति में थी।<br>बैठक में ही उस विचार को स्पष्ट शब्दों में दोबारा रखने से सुझाव का महत्व बचा रहता है और कनिष्ठ सहकर्मी का आत्मविश्वास भी, तथा प्रबंधक के अधिकार का भी सम्मान होता है।<br>चुप रहना, बाद में व्याख्यान देना या मजाक करना विचार को नहीं बचाता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): बैठक के दौरान बेहतर शब्दावली में उनके विचार को फिर से प्रस्तुत करें तथा प्रस्ताव पर पुनर्विचार का सुझाव दें।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000074088","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During dinner, your longtime childhood friend and colleague admits that they accidentally erased an important client backup file due to carelessness and intends to attribute the mistake to a recent software glitch the next day. As a peer exercising emotional intelligence, how should you respond to this situation? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"रात के भोजन के समय आपका बचपन का मित्र और सहकर्मी स्वीकार करता है कि लापरवाही के कारण उसने गलती से एक महत्वपूर्ण क्लाइंट बैकअप फ़ाइल मिटा दी है और अगले दिन वह इस गलती को हाल ही में हुई सॉफ़्टवेयर खराबी पर डालने का इरादा रखता है। एक सहकर्मी के रूप में भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का प्रयोग करते हुए आपको इस स्थिति में क्या प्रतिक्रिया देनी चाहिए? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Out of fierce loyalty to your childhood friendship, promise to back up their story and validate the software glitch theory to management.","hi":"बचपन की मित्रता के कारण उनकी कहानी का समर्थन करने का वादा करें और प्रबंधन के सामने सॉफ़्टवेयर खराबी वाले तर्क को सही ठहराएँ।"},"2":{"en":"Validate their concerns while emphasising honesty and jointly review the data to prepare a transparent remediation report.","hi":"उनकी चिंताओं को स्वीकार करें, साथ ही ईमानदारी पर जोर दें और पारदर्शी सुधार-रिपोर्ट तैयार करने के लिए मिलकर डेटा की समीक्षा करें।"},"3":{"en":"Immediately report them to HR via an anonymous email tonight to protect your own career track from any contamination.","hi":"अपने करिअर को किसी भी जोखिम से बचाने के लिए आज रात ही गुमनाम ईमेल द्वारा उनकी शिकायत मानव संसाधन विभाग से करें।"},"4":{"en":"Tell them they are incredibly foolish, mock their carelessness, and refuse to sit next to them in the office until the matter clears up.","hi":"उन्हें बहुत मूर्ख बताएँ, उनकी लापरवाही का उपहास करें और मामला साफ़ होने तक कार्यालय में उनके पास बैठने से इंकार कर दें।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Emotional intelligence means understanding the friend's panic but not supporting a lie.<br>Accepting the feelings, insisting on honesty and helping prepare a transparent report protects both the client's work and the friend's credibility.<br>Covering up the mistake, anonymous complaints or insulting the friend all make the situation worse.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Validate their concerns while emphasising honesty and jointly review the data to prepare a transparent remediation report.</b>","hi":"भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का अर्थ है मित्र की घबराहट को समझना, परंतु झूठ का साथ न देना।<br>भावनाओं को स्वीकार करना, ईमानदारी पर जोर देना और पारदर्शी रिपोर्ट बनाने में मदद करना — ये तीनों क्लाइंट के काम और मित्र की विश्वसनीयता दोनों की रक्षा करते हैं।<br>गलती छिपाना, गुमनाम शिकायत या मित्र का अपमान स्थिति को और बिगाड़ देता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): उनकी चिंताओं को स्वीकार करें, साथ ही ईमानदारी पर जोर दें और पारदर्शी सुधार-रिपोर्ट तैयार करने के लिए मिलकर डेटा की समीक्षा करें।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000074089","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern in fig. (X) by selecting one of the figures from the four alternatives :<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ea398-80e2-7276-8ae3-d6737d81bead_EN.jpg?edu=639294371617972176\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"चार विकल्पों में से एक आकृति चुनकर आकृति (X) के पैटर्न को पूर्ण कीजिए :<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ea398-80e2-7276-8ae3-d6737d81bead_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739840265\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ea39b-371a-7cb0-9b2e-7bb22ab2fc93_EN.jpg?edu=639294371617996898\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ebad3-82b0-75a0-ac1f-13c0b0d9656b_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739860300\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ea39b-371a-7cb0-9b2e-7bb3c7ca17d5_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618016982\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ebad3-82b0-75a0-ac1f-13c1fe6a7b69_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739880334\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ea39b-371a-7cb0-9b2e-7bb442fe249c_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618048941\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ebad3-82b0-75a0-ac1f-13c23675a950_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739904992\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ea39b-371a-7cb0-9b2e-7bb5f4e93e45_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618075949\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ebad3-82b0-75a0-ac1f-13c30ec07065_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739925023\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In fig. (X) the black bands run as concentric squares, each band parallel to the sides of the diamond, and the bands of the three completed quarters meet the edge of the missing quarter exactly at the corners.<br>The missing quarter must therefore repeat the same parallel bands at the same spacing and in the same direction.<br>Only option (3) continues the bands in line with the adjoining quarters; in the other options the bands turn, break or shift from the existing alignment.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3).</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) में काली पट्टियाँ संकेंद्री वर्गों के रूप में हैं, प्रत्येक पट्टी समचतुर्भुज की भुजाओं के समानांतर है, और तीनों पूर्ण भागों की पट्टियाँ लुप्त भाग के कोनों पर ठीक मिलती हैं।<br>अतः लुप्त भाग में भी उसी दूरी पर तथा उसी दिशा में समानांतर पट्टियाँ होनी चाहिए।<br>केवल विकल्प (3) में पट्टियाँ संलग्न भागों की सीध में आगे बढ़ती हैं; अन्य विकल्पों में पट्टियाँ मुड़ जाती हैं, टूट जाती हैं या संरेखण से हट जाती हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ea398-80e2-7276-8ae3-d6737d81bead_EN.jpg?edu=639294371617972176","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ea398-80e2-7276-8ae3-d6737d81bead_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739840265"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ea39b-371a-7cb0-9b2e-7bb22ab2fc93_EN.jpg?edu=639294371617996898","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ebad3-82b0-75a0-ac1f-13c0b0d9656b_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739860300"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ea39b-371a-7cb0-9b2e-7bb3c7ca17d5_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618016982","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ebad3-82b0-75a0-ac1f-13c1fe6a7b69_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739880334"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ea39b-371a-7cb0-9b2e-7bb442fe249c_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618048941","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ebad3-82b0-75a0-ac1f-13c23675a950_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739904992"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ea39b-371a-7cb0-9b2e-7bb5f4e93e45_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618075949","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ebad3-82b0-75a0-ac1f-13c30ec07065_HI.jpg?edu=639294371739925023"]}}},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000074090","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If X % Y means X is added to Y, and X π Y means X is multiplied by Y, find the expression for “the sum of A and B multiplied by the value of C.” [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि X % Y का अर्थ है X को Y में जोड़ा जाता है, तथा X π Y का अर्थ है X को Y से गुणा किया जाता है, तो “A और B का योगफल, C के मान से गुणा” के लिए व्यंजक ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(A % B) π C"},"2":{"en":"A % (B π C)"},"3":{"en":"(A π B) % C"},"4":{"en":"A π B π C"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"% stands for addition and π stands for multiplication.<br>“The sum of A and B” is written as (A % B).<br>This sum is then multiplied by C, so the multiplication is done on the bracket: (A % B) π C.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): (A % B) π C.</b>","hi":"% जोड़ को तथा π गुणा को दर्शाता है।<br>“A और B का योगफल” को (A % B) लिखा जाएगा।<br>इस योगफल को C से गुणा किया जाना है, इसलिए गुणा कोष्ठक पर होगा: (A % B) π C.<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): (A % B) π C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000074091","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 12 × 3 means 4, 15 − 5 means 75, and 4 ÷ 2 means 6, then what is the value of 20 − 10 × 5 ÷ 2? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि 12 × 3 का अर्थ 4 है, 15 − 5 का अर्थ 75 है और 4 ÷ 2 का अर्थ 6 है, तो 20 − 10 × 5 ÷ 2 का मान क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"38"},"2":{"en":"42"},"3":{"en":"56"},"4":{"en":"62"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"12 × 3 = 4 means 12 ÷ 3 = 4, so × stands for ÷.<br>15 − 5 = 75 means 15 × 5 = 75, so − stands for ×.<br>4 ÷ 2 = 6 means 4 + 2 = 6, so ÷ stands for +.<br>Now 20 − 10 × 5 ÷ 2 becomes 20 × 10 ÷ 5 + 2.<br>By BODMAS: 20 × 10 = 200, 200 ÷ 5 = 40, 40 + 2 = <b>42</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 42.</b>","hi":"12 × 3 = 4 का अर्थ 12 ÷ 3 = 4 है, अर्थात् × का अर्थ ÷ है।<br>15 − 5 = 75 का अर्थ 15 × 5 = 75 है, अर्थात् − का अर्थ × है।<br>4 ÷ 2 = 6 का अर्थ 4 + 2 = 6 है, अर्थात् ÷ का अर्थ + है।<br>अब 20 − 10 × 5 ÷ 2 बनता है 20 × 10 ÷ 5 + 2।<br>BODMAS के अनुसार: 20 × 10 = 200, 200 ÷ 5 = 40, 40 + 2 = <b>42</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 42 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000074092","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement. <b>Statement:</b><br>Pedestrians crossing busy roads without using designated zebra crossings often disrupt traffic movement and increase the chances of accidents during peak hours.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. Improper road crossing can create safety hazards.<br>II. Only pedestrians are responsible for road accidents. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन दिया गया है, जिसके बाद कुछ निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, चाहे वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों का विरोध करता प्रतीत हो। निष्कर्षों को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और निर्णय लीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से दिए गए कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं। <b>कथन:</b><br>जो पैदल यात्री निर्धारित जेबरा क्रॉसिंग का उपयोग किए बिना व्यस्त सड़कें पार करते हैं, वे अक्सर यातायात को बाधित करते हैं और व्यस्त समय में दुर्घटनाओं की संभावना बढ़ा देते हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. अनुचित तरीके से सड़क पार करना सुरक्षा के लिए खतरा उत्पन्न कर सकता है।<br>II. सड़क दुर्घटनाओं के लिए केवल पैदल यात्री ही उत्तरदायी हैं। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The statement says crossing without a zebra crossing increases the chance of accidents, so improper crossing does create a safety hazard — Inference I follows.<br>The statement speaks only about pedestrians and says nothing about who else causes accidents, so Inference II (“only pedestrians”) is too broad and does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Inference I follows.</b>","hi":"कथन कहता है कि जेबरा क्रॉसिंग के बिना सड़क पार करने से दुर्घटना की संभावना बढ़ती है, अतः अनुचित तरीके से सड़क पार करना सुरक्षा के लिए खतरा है — निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।<br>कथन केवल पैदल यात्रियों के बारे में है और यह नहीं बताता कि दुर्घटनाओं के लिए अन्य कौन उत्तरदायी है, अतः निष्कर्ष II (“केवल पैदल यात्री”) अत्यधिक व्यापक है और नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000074093","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"If a mirror is placed on the line MN, which figure will be the mirror image of the question figure?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eba28-8143-728c-8c07-541ba784fff7_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618659476\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि रेखा MN पर दर्पण रखा जाए, तो प्रश्न आकृति का दर्पण प्रतिबिंब कौन-सी आकृति होगी?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019eba28-8143-728c-8c07-541ba784fff7_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740401607\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eba32-3103-7235-9b80-9044d9db2344_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618695827\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f035c-68ed-7a6c-aeef-a7cd767790e3_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740429060\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eba32-3103-7235-9b80-90458cfc4dc9_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618734042\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f035c-68ed-7a6c-aeef-a7ceb745ce85_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740456940\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eba32-3103-7235-9b80-90465480d040_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618770992\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f035c-68ed-7a6c-aeef-a7cf5ed93de2_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740488826\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eba32-3103-7235-9b80-904770541d12_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618811084\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f035c-68ed-7a6c-aeef-a7d06349fa52_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740517071\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"MN is a vertical mirror, so the mirror image reverses the order of the characters from left to right and turns each character sideways (lateral inversion).<br>The group 5 y r 7 4 h therefore reads, from the left, as the inverted h, then 4, then 7, then r, then y and finally the inverted 5.<br>Only option (3) shows all six characters inverted and in exactly this order.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3).</b>","hi":"MN ऊर्ध्वाधर दर्पण है, इसलिए दर्पण प्रतिबिंब में अक्षरों का क्रम बाएँ से दाएँ उलट जाता है और प्रत्येक अक्षर पार्श्वतः उलटा (lateral inversion) हो जाता है।<br>अतः समूह 5 y r 7 4 h बाएँ से पढ़ने पर इस प्रकार होगा — उलटा h, फिर 4, फिर 7, फिर r, फिर y और अंत में उलटा 5।<br>केवल विकल्प (3) में सभी छह अक्षर उलटे हुए तथा ठीक इसी क्रम में हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eba28-8143-728c-8c07-541ba784fff7_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618659476","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019eba28-8143-728c-8c07-541ba784fff7_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740401607"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eba32-3103-7235-9b80-9044d9db2344_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618695827","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f035c-68ed-7a6c-aeef-a7cd767790e3_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740429060"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eba32-3103-7235-9b80-90458cfc4dc9_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618734042","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f035c-68ed-7a6c-aeef-a7ceb745ce85_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740456940"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eba32-3103-7235-9b80-90465480d040_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618770992","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f035c-68ed-7a6c-aeef-a7cf5ed93de2_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740488826"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eba32-3103-7235-9b80-904770541d12_EN.jpg?edu=639294371618811084","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f035c-68ed-7a6c-aeef-a7d06349fa52_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740517071"]}}},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000074094","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A client requests a specific feature for their software project that is outside the original project scope. Your manager is away, and the client is pressuring you to commit to the deadline today. What should you do? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक क्लाइंट अपने सॉफ़्टवेयर प्रोजेक्ट के लिए एक ऐसी विशेष सुविधा मांगता है, जो मूल प्रोजेक्ट के दायरे से बाहर है। आपके प्रबंधक बाहर गए हैं और क्लाइंट आज ही समय-सीमा तय करने के लिए दबाव डाल रहा है। आपको क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Agree to the request immediately to keep the client happy.","hi":"क्लाइंट को प्रसन्न रखने के लिए तुरंत अनुरोध स्वीकार कर लें।"},"2":{"en":"Refuse the request flatly to avoid extra work.","hi":"अतिरिक्त कार्य से बचने के लिए अनुरोध सीधे मना कर दें।"},"3":{"en":"Acknowledge the request, consult your manager, and provide an update by day end.","hi":"अनुरोध स्वीकार करें, अपने प्रबंधक से परामर्श करें और दिन के अंत तक जानकारी दें।"},"4":{"en":"Do the work in secret so that it does not show on the official project logs.","hi":"कार्य चुपचाप कर लें ताकि वह आधिकारिक प्रोजेक्ट लॉग में दर्ज न हो।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A request outside the agreed scope changes cost and time, so it is not for the executive to promise alone.<br>Acknowledging the request keeps the client engaged, consulting the manager keeps the commitment realistic, and a reply by the day's end fits the client's urgency.<br>Agreeing at once, refusing flatly or doing secret work all create risk.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Acknowledge the request, consult your manager, and provide an update by day end.</b>","hi":"सहमत दायरे से बाहर का अनुरोध लागत और समय बदल देता है, अतः उसे अकेले वादा करना अधिकारी के लिए उचित नहीं।<br>अनुरोध स्वीकार करना क्लाइंट को जोड़े रखता है, प्रबंधक से परामर्श करना प्रतिबद्धता को यथार्थपरक बनाता है, और दिन के अंत तक उत्तर देना क्लाइंट की तात्कालिकता के अनुरूप है।<br>तुरंत हामी भरना, सीधे मना करना या गुप्त रूप से कार्य करना — तीनों जोखिम पैदा करते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): अनुरोध स्वीकार करें, अपने प्रबंधक से परामर्श करें और दिन के अंत तक जानकारी दें।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000074095","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br>Question Figures:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed373-9a18-701e-b04d-066849bd3ddb_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619099674\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनकर तीसरी और चौथी आकृति के बीच भी वैसा ही संबंध स्थापित कीजिए, जो प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर आएगी।<br>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ed373-9a18-701e-b04d-066849bd3ddb_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740745884\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In the first figure the small circle lies on the left of a vertical line and the arrow below it points down; in the second figure the whole arrangement is turned upside down, the circle moves to the right of the line and the arrow now points up, while the two dots stay below the line.<br>Applying the same change to the third figure (V-shaped figure with dots and a circle at the bottom right), the figure must be inverted so that the circle comes at the bottom left, the two dots lie on the left and the open side of the V faces upwards.<br>Answer figure (3) shows exactly this inverted arrangement.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3.</b>","hi":"पहली आकृति में छोटा वृत्त एक ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखा के बाईं ओर है और उसके नीचे तीर नीचे की ओर है; दूसरी आकृति में पूरी व्यवस्था उलट दी गई है, वृत्त रेखा के दाईं ओर चला जाता है और तीर अब ऊपर की ओर है, जबकि दो बिंदु रेखा के नीचे ही रहते हैं।<br>यही परिवर्तन तीसरी आकृति (V जैसी आकृति, जिसमें बिंदु तथा नीचे दाईं ओर वृत्त है) पर लागू करने पर आकृति उलटी हो जाएगी, वृत्त नीचे बाईं ओर आ जाएगा, दो बिंदु बाईं ओर होंगे और V की खुली भुजा ऊपर की ओर होगी।<br>उत्तर आकृति (3) में ठीक यही उलटी व्यवस्था दिखाई गई है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed373-9a18-701e-b04d-066849bd3ddb_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619099674","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ed373-9a18-701e-b04d-066849bd3ddb_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740745884"]}},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000074096","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br>Question Figures:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed384-af9e-76ea-b09f-53d5bd26bf23_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619336130\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनकर तीसरी और चौथी आकृति के बीच भी वैसा ही संबंध स्थापित कीजिए, जो प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर आएगी।<br>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ed384-af9e-76ea-b09f-53d5bd26bf23_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740930571\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The first two figures are the same triangle pattern inside a square, the second only being the first rotated through 180<sup>o</sup>.<br>The third figure is an inverted V with a small triangle inside and a horizontal bar at the bottom; turning it through 180<sup>o</sup> gives an upright A-shaped figure with the small triangle at the top and the bar above it.<br>Answer figure (2) shows this upright A-shaped figure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"पहली दो आकृतियाँ एक वर्ग के भीतर वही त्रिभुज-पैटर्न हैं, दूसरी आकृति पहली को 180<sup>o</sup> घुमाकर प्राप्त होती है।<br>तीसरी आकृति उलटी V है, जिसके भीतर छोटा त्रिभुज और नीचे क्षैतिज पट्टी है; इसे 180<sup>o</sup> घुमाने पर सीधी A जैसी आकृति बनती है, जिसमें छोटा त्रिभुज ऊपर और पट्टी उसके ऊपर होती है।<br>उत्तर आकृति (2) में यही सीधी A जैसी आकृति है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed384-af9e-76ea-b09f-53d5bd26bf23_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619336130","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ed384-af9e-76ea-b09f-53d5bd26bf23_HI.jpg?edu=639294371740930571"]}},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000074097","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"Carefully observe Figure (X) and identify the option figure in which Figure (X) is embedded exactly as shown.<br>Figure X:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed589-528c-70c7-8da2-634636e43ce3_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619581852\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) को ध्यानपूर्वक देखिए और वह विकल्प आकृति पहचानिए जिसमें आकृति (X) ठीक वैसे ही अंतर्निहित है जैसी दिखाई गई है।<br>आकृति X:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ed589-528c-70c7-8da2-634636e43ce3_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741143309\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed58c-a9bd-798f-baad-2518f174a624_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619628990\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0304-0143-707b-bd02-8c8f535053e5_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741179129\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed58c-a9bd-798f-baad-2519df920fe2_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619669119\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0304-0143-707b-bd02-8c903cf083af_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741217538\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed58c-a9bd-798f-baad-251a690285d4_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619727927\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0304-0143-707b-bd02-8c91f31af004_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741253341\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed58c-a9bd-798f-baad-251b313e52c0_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619780635\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0304-0143-707b-bd02-8c922914986f_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741293435\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is a circle with two straight cuts meeting at a point on the circumference, forming a narrow V-shaped mouth towards the upper right.<br>The option figure must contain this circle with the same V-shaped mouth in the same position (rotation is not allowed).<br>In options (1) and (3) the circle is cut by a vertical and a horizontal line, and in option (2) by two crossing diagonals, so the V-shaped mouth is not present there; only option (4) contains the circle with the required V-cut.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4).</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) एक वृत्त है, जिसमें परिधि के एक बिंदु पर मिलती हुई दो सीधी रेखाएँ ऊपर-दाईं ओर संकरा V-आकार का मुख बनाती हैं।<br>विकल्प आकृति में यही वृत्त उसी स्थिति में उसी V-आकार के मुख के साथ अंतर्निहित होना चाहिए (घुमाने की अनुमति नहीं है)।<br>विकल्प (1) और (3) में वृत्त ऊर्ध्वाधर तथा क्षैतिज रेखाओं से कटा है और विकल्प (2) में दो क्रॉस करती विकर्णों से, अतः वहाँ V-आकार का मुख नहीं है; केवल विकल्प (4) में वृत्त के साथ आवश्यक V-कट है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed589-528c-70c7-8da2-634636e43ce3_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619581852","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019ed589-528c-70c7-8da2-634636e43ce3_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741143309"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed58c-a9bd-798f-baad-2518f174a624_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619628990","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0304-0143-707b-bd02-8c8f535053e5_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741179129"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed58c-a9bd-798f-baad-2519df920fe2_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619669119","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0304-0143-707b-bd02-8c903cf083af_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741217538"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed58c-a9bd-798f-baad-251a690285d4_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619727927","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0304-0143-707b-bd02-8c91f31af004_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741253341"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed58c-a9bd-798f-baad-251b313e52c0_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619780635","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0304-0143-707b-bd02-8c922914986f_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741293435"]}}},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000074098","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Which of the following Venn diagram represents the relationship between “Educated”, “Employed” and “Urban”? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा वेन आरेख “Educated”, “Employed” तथा “Urban” के बीच का संबंध दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed99c-f27c-7196-9974-d93604f1e137_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619894876\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0282-1d72-7139-8d92-97636011317f_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741383435\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed99c-f27c-7196-9974-d93735895b94_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619950330\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0282-1d72-7139-8d92-9764a99b16cf_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741431185\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed99c-f27c-7196-9974-d9383b45c214_EN.jpg?edu=639294371620000287\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0282-1d72-7139-8d92-9765b9e74078_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741471306\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed99c-f27c-7196-9974-d939dee61d1f_EN.jpg?edu=639294371620052237\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0282-1d72-7139-8d92-97661aca9fc6_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741515724\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A person may be educated and employed at the same time, educated and living in an urban area, employed and living in an urban area, or all three together.<br>At the same time each of the three groups has members who do not belong to the other two, so no circle lies wholly inside another.<br>Hence the three sets overlap each other partially — three intersecting circles — which is option (3).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3).</b>","hi":"कोई व्यक्ति एक साथ शिक्षित और नियोजित हो सकता है, शिक्षित और शहरी क्षेत्र में रहने वाला हो सकता है, नियोजित और शहरी हो सकता है, अथवा तीनों हो सकता है।<br>साथ ही तीनों समूहों में ऐसे सदस्य भी हैं जो अन्य दो में नहीं आते, इसलिए कोई वृत्त पूरी तरह दूसरे के भीतर नहीं है।<br>अतः तीनों समुच्चय आंशिक रूप से एक-दूसरे को काटते हैं — तीन प्रतिच्छेदी वृत्त — जो विकल्प (3) है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed99c-f27c-7196-9974-d93604f1e137_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619894876","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0282-1d72-7139-8d92-97636011317f_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741383435"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed99c-f27c-7196-9974-d93735895b94_EN.jpg?edu=639294371619950330","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0282-1d72-7139-8d92-9764a99b16cf_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741431185"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed99c-f27c-7196-9974-d9383b45c214_EN.jpg?edu=639294371620000287","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0282-1d72-7139-8d92-9765b9e74078_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741471306"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019ed99c-f27c-7196-9974-d939dee61d1f_EN.jpg?edu=639294371620052237","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f0282-1d72-7139-8d92-97661aca9fc6_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741515724"]}}},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000074099","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eda47-2664-76a9-918b-eefc9fad024c_EN.jpg?edu=639294371620123864\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c), (d) तथा (e) से अंकित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी एक प्रकार से समान हैं। परंतु एक आकृति अन्य चारों जैसी नहीं है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो शेष से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019eda47-2664-76a9-918b-eefc9fad024c_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741566432\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"a"},"2":{"en":"c"},"3":{"en":"d"},"4":{"en":"e"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In figures (a), (b), (c) and (e) the dot lies on the boundary of the square, exactly at one of its corners.<br>In figure (d) the dot lies inside the square, away from the boundary, so the dot is not placed at a corner.<br>Thus figure (d) is different from the other four.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): d.</b>","hi":"आकृति (a), (b), (c) तथा (e) में बिंदु वर्ग की परिसीमा पर, ठीक उसके किसी एक कोने पर स्थित है।<br>आकृति (d) में बिंदु वर्ग के भीतर, परिसीमा से हटकर है, अर्थात् बिंदु किसी कोने पर नहीं है।<br>इस प्रकार आकृति (d) अन्य चारों से भिन्न है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): d है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019eda47-2664-76a9-918b-eefc9fad024c_EN.jpg?edu=639294371620123864","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019eda47-2664-76a9-918b-eefc9fad024c_HI.jpg?edu=639294371741566432"]}},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000074100","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The government is considering a complete ban on single-use plastic bags in all retail outlets to protect the local environment.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Retail outlets are the largest source of plastic waste in the region.<br>II. Eliminating plastic bags will lead to a cleaner and healthier local environment. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिया गया कथन तथा उस पर आधारित अधोलिखित पूर्वधारणाएँ ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए। निर्णय लीजिए कि कौन-सी पूर्वधारणाएँ कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>स्थानीय पर्यावरण की सुरक्षा के लिए सरकार सभी खुदरा दुकानों में सिंगल-यूज़ प्लास्टिक बैग पर पूर्ण प्रतिबंध लगाने पर विचार कर रही है।<br><b>पूर्वधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. खुदरा दुकानें इस क्षेत्र में प्लास्टिक कचरे का सबसे बड़ा स्रोत हैं।<br>II. प्लास्टिक बैग समाप्त करने से स्थानीय पर्यावरण स्वच्छ और स्वस्थ होगा। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल पूर्वधारणा I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"पूर्वधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल पूर्वधारणा II निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो पूर्वधारणा I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The purpose stated in the statement is to protect the local environment, so the government must be assuming that removing plastic bags will make the environment cleaner and healthier — Assumption II is implicit.<br>Nothing in the statement compares retail outlets with other sources of plastic waste, so Assumption I is not implicit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only Assumption II is implicit.</b>","hi":"कथन में बताया गया उद्देश्य स्थानीय पर्यावरण की सुरक्षा है, अतः सरकार यह मानकर चल रही है कि प्लास्टिक बैग हटाने से पर्यावरण स्वच्छ और स्वस्थ होगा — पूर्वधारणा II निहित है।<br>कथन में खुदरा दुकानों की तुलना प्लास्टिक कचरे के अन्य स्रोतों से कहीं नहीं की गई, अतः पूर्वधारणा I निहित नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल पूर्वधारणा II निहित है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000074101","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"Four different positions of the same dice are shown. Select the number that will be on the face opposite to the one showing ‘3’.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019edaa6-a948-73a8-afe2-13ef03476d67_EN.jpg?edu=639294371620738382\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक ही पासे की चार अलग-अलग स्थितियाँ दिखाई गई हैं। उस अंक का चयन कीजिए जो ‘3’ दर्शाने वाले फलक के विपरीत फलक पर होगा।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019edaa6-a948-73a8-afe2-13ef03476d67_HI.jpg?edu=639294371742050174\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the four positions the faces next to 3 are:<br>First position: 3 with 7 and 5<br>Second position: 3 with 5 and 2<br>Third position: 3 with 4 and 1<br>Fourth position: 3 with 4 and 2<br>So the faces adjacent to 3 are 7, 5, 2, 4 and 1.<br>The only number left is 6, so 6 lies opposite 3.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 6.</b>","hi":"चारों स्थितियों से 3 के साथ आने वाले फलक हैं:<br>पहली स्थिति: 3 के साथ 7 और 5<br>दूसरी स्थिति: 3 के साथ 5 और 2<br>तीसरी स्थिति: 3 के साथ 4 और 1<br>चौथी स्थिति: 3 के साथ 4 और 2<br>अतः 3 के निकटवर्ती फलक हैं 7, 5, 2, 4 तथा 1।<br>शेष बचता है केवल 6, इसलिए 3 के विपरीत फलक पर 6 होगा।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 6 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019edaa6-a948-73a8-afe2-13ef03476d67_EN.jpg?edu=639294371620738382","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019edaa6-a948-73a8-afe2-13ef03476d67_HI.jpg?edu=639294371742050174"]}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000074102","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019edb88-04af-7a72-a179-3c2128a9c63a_EN.jpg?edu=639294371621069784\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c), (d) तथा (e) से अंकित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी एक प्रकार से समान हैं। परंतु एक आकृति अन्य चारों जैसी नहीं है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो शेष से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019edb88-04af-7a72-a179-3c2128a9c63a_HI.jpg?edu=639294371742311939\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"c"},"2":{"en":"d"},"3":{"en":"a"},"4":{"en":"e"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Each square is cut into eight equal triangles by its two diagonals and its two middle lines, and two of these triangles are shaded.<br>In figures (a), (b), (c) and (e) the two shaded triangles share one of the lines drawn from the centre, so together they form a single continuous triangle occupying one-fourth of the square.<br>In figure (d) the two shaded triangles meet only at the centre point and together do not form one continuous triangle, so its shading is different from the rest.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): d.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक वर्ग अपने दो विकर्णों तथा दो मध्य रेखाओं से आठ समान त्रिभुजों में बँटा है और इनमें से दो त्रिभुज छायांकित हैं।<br>आकृति (a), (b), (c) तथा (e) में दोनों छायांकित त्रिभुज केंद्र से खींची गई एक ही रेखा साझा करते हैं, अतः मिलकर वे वर्ग का एक-चौथाई भाग घेरने वाला एक सतत त्रिभुज बनाते हैं।<br>आकृति (d) में दोनों छायांकित त्रिभुज केवल केंद्र बिंदु पर मिलते हैं और मिलकर एक सतत त्रिभुज नहीं बनाते, इसलिए इसका छायांकन शेष से भिन्न है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): d है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019edb88-04af-7a72-a179-3c2128a9c63a_EN.jpg?edu=639294371621069784","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019edb88-04af-7a72-a179-3c2128a9c63a_HI.jpg?edu=639294371742311939"]}},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000074103","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\" colspan=\"5\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">17</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">17</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी प्रकार एक-दूसरे से जुड़े/संबंधित हैं?<br><table><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\" colspan=\"5\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">17</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">17</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Columns I, II and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, II तथा IV"},"2":{"en":"Columns I, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, III तथा IV"},"3":{"en":"Columns I, II and III","hi":"स्तंभ I, II तथा III"},"4":{"en":"Columns I, III and V","hi":"स्तंभ I, III तथा V"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Check the columns in every row:<br>Row I: 4 + 3 = 7 (column II) and 11 − 2 = 9 (column IV)<br>Row II: 8 + 3 = 11 and 15 − 2 = 13<br>Row III: 6 + 3 = 9 and 13 − 2 = 11<br>Row IV: 12 + 3 = 15 and 20 − 2 = 17<br>Row V: 10 + 3 = 13 and 17 − 2 = 15<br>Column II is always column I + 3 and column IV is always column III − 2, so columns I, II and IV are related.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Columns I, II and IV.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में स्तंभों की जाँच कीजिए:<br>पंक्ति I: 4 + 3 = 7 (स्तंभ II) तथा 11 − 2 = 9 (स्तंभ IV)<br>पंक्ति II: 8 + 3 = 11 तथा 15 − 2 = 13<br>पंक्ति III: 6 + 3 = 9 तथा 13 − 2 = 11<br>पंक्ति IV: 12 + 3 = 15 तथा 20 − 2 = 17<br>पंक्ति V: 10 + 3 = 13 तथा 17 − 2 = 15<br>स्तंभ II सदैव स्तंभ I + 3 है और स्तंभ IV सदैव स्तंभ III − 2 है, अतः स्तंभ I, II तथा IV संबंधित हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): स्तंभ I, II तथा IV है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000074104","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks (_) using one of the following four options such that the series follows a specific order.<br>c_bdca_dcab__abd [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"रिक्त स्थानों (_) को निम्नलिखित चार विकल्पों में से एक से भरिए, जिससे श्रृंखला एक निश्चित क्रम का पालन करे।<br>c_bdca_dcab__abd [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"adbc"},"2":{"en":"cbad"},"3":{"en":"abdc"},"4":{"en":"abcd"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Put the letters of each option in the four blanks and read the series.<br>With abdc: c<b>a</b>bd ca<b>b</b>d cab<b>d</b><b>c</b>abd = cabd cabd cabd cabd<br>The group cabd repeats four times, so the series follows a fixed order.<br>The other options break the repetition of the group.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): abdc.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक विकल्प के अक्षर चारों रिक्त स्थानों में रखकर श्रृंखला पढ़िए।<br>abdc रखने पर: c<b>a</b>bd ca<b>b</b>d cab<b>d</b><b>c</b>abd = cabd cabd cabd cabd<br>समूह cabd चार बार दोहराया जाता है, अतः श्रृंखला एक निश्चित क्रम का पालन करती है।<br>अन्य विकल्पों में समूह की यह पुनरावृत्ति टूट जाती है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): abdc है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000074105","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Select a figure from among the alternatives that will continue the same series established by the Problem Figures.<br>Problem Figures:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f1d72-8690-7739-b118-a49198949967_EN.jpg?edu=639294371622211142\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"विकल्पों में से वह आकृति चुनिए जो प्रश्न आकृतियों द्वारा स्थापित उसी श्रृंखला को आगे बढ़ाएगी।<br>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f1d72-8690-7739-b118-a49198949967_HI.jpg?edu=639294371743142085\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f1d88-931f-777a-aec8-698964f8ce5f_EN.jpg?edu=639294371622287259\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f4a92-8514-770f-9326-59879dafa008_HI.jpg?edu=639294371743198406\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f1d88-931f-777a-aec8-698a68efd135_EN.jpg?edu=639294371622346684\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f4a92-8514-770f-9326-5988b1a1c9ee_HI.jpg?edu=639294371743255383\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f1d88-931f-777a-aec8-698b55dda3c8_EN.jpg?edu=639294371622431366\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f4a92-8514-770f-9326-5989f21d432f_HI.jpg?edu=639294371743307289\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f1d88-931f-777a-aec8-698cd0b59dae_EN.jpg?edu=639294371622501851\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f4a92-8514-770f-9326-598ab21f11c4_HI.jpg?edu=639294371743364506\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the problem figures the whole arrangement turns through 90<sup>o</sup> at every step: the small circle moves from the top-right to the top-left, then to the bottom-left, and the arrow keeps turning with it in the same direction.<br>The fourth figure therefore has the circle at the bottom-left and the arrow pointing to the right at the top-right corner.<br>Only option (4) shows the arrangement in exactly this position.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4).</b>","hi":"प्रश्न आकृतियों में पूरी व्यवस्था प्रत्येक चरण पर 90<sup>o</sup> घूमती है: छोटा वृत्त ऊपर-दाएँ से ऊपर-बाएँ और फिर नीचे-बाएँ चला जाता है, तथा तीर भी उसी दिशा में साथ-साथ घूमता रहता है।<br>अतः चौथी आकृति में वृत्त नीचे-बाएँ कोने में होगा और तीर ऊपर-दाएँ कोने पर दाईं ओर संकेत करेगा।<br>केवल विकल्प (4) में व्यवस्था ठीक इसी स्थिति में है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f1d72-8690-7739-b118-a49198949967_EN.jpg?edu=639294371622211142","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f1d72-8690-7739-b118-a49198949967_HI.jpg?edu=639294371743142085"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f1d88-931f-777a-aec8-698964f8ce5f_EN.jpg?edu=639294371622287259","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f4a92-8514-770f-9326-59879dafa008_HI.jpg?edu=639294371743198406"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f1d88-931f-777a-aec8-698a68efd135_EN.jpg?edu=639294371622346684","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f4a92-8514-770f-9326-5988b1a1c9ee_HI.jpg?edu=639294371743255383"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f1d88-931f-777a-aec8-698b55dda3c8_EN.jpg?edu=639294371622431366","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f4a92-8514-770f-9326-5989f21d432f_HI.jpg?edu=639294371743307289"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f1d88-931f-777a-aec8-698cd0b59dae_EN.jpg?edu=639294371622501851","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f4a92-8514-770f-9326-598ab21f11c4_HI.jpg?edu=639294371743364506"]}}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000074106","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Constitutional and Non-Constitutional Bodies","question":{"en":"The Finance Commission of India is constituted by the President under which Article? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत का वित्त आयोग राष्ट्रपति द्वारा किस अनुच्छेद के तहत गठित किया जाता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 280","hi":"अनुच्छेद 280"},"2":{"en":"Article 148","hi":"अनुच्छेद 148"},"3":{"en":"Article 324","hi":"अनुच्छेद 324"},"4":{"en":"Article 315","hi":"अनुच्छेद 315"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Article 280</b><br>Under <b><u>Article 280</u></b>, the President constitutes a <b>Finance Commission</b> every <b>five years</b> (or earlier) to recommend the distribution of taxes between the Centre and the States.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It has a Chairman and <b>four other members</b>; first FC chaired by <b>K.C. Neogy</b> (1951).<br>• <b>16<sup>th</sup> FC</b> is chaired by <b>Arvind Panagariya</b>.<br>• <b>Art. 148</b> – CAG; <b>Art. 324</b> – Election Commission; <b>Art. 315</b> – Public Service Commissions.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अनुच्छेद 280</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 280</u></b> के तहत राष्ट्रपति हर <b>पाँच वर्ष</b> (या पहले) केंद्र और राज्यों के बीच करों के वितरण की सिफारिश के लिए <b>वित्त आयोग</b> का गठन करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसमें एक अध्यक्ष और <b>चार अन्य सदस्य</b> होते हैं; पहले वित्त आयोग के अध्यक्ष <b>के.सी. नियोगी</b> (1951)।<br>• <b>16वें वित्त आयोग</b> के अध्यक्ष <b>अरविंद पनगढ़िया</b> हैं।<br>• <b>अनु. 148</b> – CAG; <b>अनु. 324</b> – निर्वाचन आयोग; <b>अनु. 315</b> – लोक सेवा आयोग।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000074107","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Constitutional and Non-Constitutional Bodies","question":{"en":"Which Article provides for the establishment of the Union Public Service Commission? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-सा अनुच्छेद संघ लोक सेवा आयोग की स्थापना का प्रावधान करता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 315 of the Indian Constitution","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 315"},"2":{"en":"Article 320 of the Indian Constitution","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 320"},"3":{"en":"Article 323 of the Indian Constitution","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 323"},"4":{"en":"Article 324 of the Indian Constitution","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 324"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Article 315 of the Indian Constitution</b><br><b><u>Article 315</u></b> provides that there shall be a <b>Public Service Commission for the Union</b> and one for each State.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• UPSC provisions: <b>Part XIV, Articles 315–323</b>.<br>• <b>Art. 320</b> – functions of PSCs; <b>Art. 323</b> – annual reports of PSCs.<br>• UPSC members hold office for <b>6 years or till 65 years</b> of age.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 315</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 315</u></b> के अनुसार <b>संघ के लिए एक लोक सेवा आयोग</b> और प्रत्येक राज्य के लिए एक लोक सेवा आयोग होगा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• UPSC प्रावधान: <b>भाग XIV, अनुच्छेद 315–323</b>।<br>• <b>अनु. 320</b> – लोक सेवा आयोगों के कार्य; <b>अनु. 323</b> – वार्षिक प्रतिवेदन।<br>• UPSC सदस्य <b>6 वर्ष या 65 वर्ष की आयु</b> तक पद पर रहते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000074108","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: India and Its Location","question":{"en":"How much time difference exists between the westernmost village of Gujarat and Walong in Arunachal Pradesh? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"गुजरात के सबसे पश्चिमी गाँव और अरुणाचल प्रदेश के वालोंग के बीच कितना समय अंतर है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 hour","hi":"1 घंटा"},"2":{"en":"2 hours","hi":"2 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"3 hours","hi":"3 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"½ hour","hi":"½ घंटा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 2 hours</b><br>India extends from about <b>68°7′ E (Gujarat)</b> to <b>97°25′ E (Arunachal Pradesh)</b> – about 30° of longitude.<br>1° = 4 minutes, so 30° × 4 = 120 minutes = <b><u>2 hours</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Because of this difference, <b>IST (82°30′ E)</b> is used as the standard meridian.<br>• Westernmost point: <b>Guhar Moti (Kutch)</b>; easternmost: <b>Kibithu (Arunachal)</b>.<br>• East–west extent of India is about <b>2,933 km</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 2 घंटे</b><br>भारत लगभग <b>68°7′ पूर्व (गुजरात)</b> से <b>97°25′ पूर्व (अरुणाचल प्रदेश)</b> तक फैला है – लगभग 30° देशांतर।<br>1° = 4 मिनट, अतः 30° × 4 = 120 मिनट = <b><u>2 घंटे</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस अंतर के कारण <b>IST (82°30′ पूर्व)</b> को मानक याम्योत्तर माना गया है।<br>• सबसे पश्चिमी बिंदु: <b>गुहार मोती (कच्छ)</b>; सबसे पूर्वी: <b>किबिथु (अरुणाचल)</b>।<br>• भारत का पूर्व–पश्चिम विस्तार लगभग <b>2,933 km</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000074109","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Supreme Court and High Court","question":{"en":"What is the subject matter of Article 126 of the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 126 का विषय क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Appointment of Supreme Court judges","hi":"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीशों की नियुक्ति"},"2":{"en":"Powers of the Chief Justice of India","hi":"भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश की शक्तियाँ"},"3":{"en":"Appointment of Acting Chief Justice","hi":"कार्यवाहक मुख्य न्यायाधीश की नियुक्ति"},"4":{"en":"Retirement of judges of the Supreme Court","hi":"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीशों की सेवानिवृत्ति"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Appointment of Acting Chief Justice</b><br><b>Article 126</b> empowers the President to appoint a judge of the Supreme Court as the <b><u>acting Chief Justice of India</u></b> when the office of CJI is vacant or the CJI is absent.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Art. 124</b> – establishment and constitution of the Supreme Court; judges retire at <b>65</b>.<br>• <b>Art. 127</b> – ad hoc judges; <b>Art. 128</b> – retired judges at sittings.<br>• <b>Art. 129</b> – Supreme Court as a court of record.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कार्यवाहक मुख्य न्यायाधीश की नियुक्ति</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 126</b> मुख्य न्यायाधीश का पद रिक्त होने या उनकी अनुपस्थिति में राष्ट्रपति को सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के किसी न्यायाधीश को <b><u>कार्यवाहक मुख्य न्यायाधीश</u></b> नियुक्त करने का अधिकार देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनु. 124</b> – सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की स्थापना और गठन; न्यायाधीश <b>65</b> वर्ष में सेवानिवृत्त।<br>• <b>अनु. 127</b> – तदर्थ न्यायाधीश; <b>अनु. 128</b> – सेवानिवृत्त न्यायाधीशों की उपस्थिति।<br>• <b>अनु. 129</b> – सर्वोच्च न्यायालय अभिलेख न्यायालय।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000074110","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Supreme Court and High Court","question":{"en":"Which article of the Constitution of India empowers a High Court to issue writs? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत के संविधान का कौन-सा अनुच्छेद उच्च न्यायालय को रिट जारी करने का अधिकार देता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 226","hi":"अनुच्छेद 226"},"2":{"en":"Article 32","hi":"अनुच्छेद 32"},"3":{"en":"Article 132","hi":"अनुच्छेद 132"},"4":{"en":"Article 270","hi":"अनुच्छेद 270"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Article 226</b><br><b><u>Article 226</u></b> empowers High Courts to issue writs for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights and <b>\"for any other purpose\"</b>, so its scope is wider than Article 32.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Art. 32</b> – writ jurisdiction of the Supreme Court (a Fundamental Right).<br>• <b>Art. 132</b> – appellate jurisdiction of SC in constitutional cases.<br>• <b>Art. 270</b> – taxes levied and distributed between Union and States.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अनुच्छेद 226</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 226</u></b> उच्च न्यायालयों को मौलिक अधिकारों के प्रवर्तन तथा <b>\"किसी अन्य प्रयोजन\"</b> के लिए रिट जारी करने का अधिकार देता है, अतः इसका दायरा अनुच्छेद 32 से व्यापक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनु. 32</b> – सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का रिट क्षेत्राधिकार (मौलिक अधिकार)।<br>• <b>अनु. 132</b> – संवैधानिक मामलों में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का अपीलीय क्षेत्राधिकार।<br>• <b>अनु. 270</b> – संघ द्वारा लगाए और राज्यों में वितरित कर।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000074111","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"For which of the following physical quantities is the SI unit the candela? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किस भौतिक राशि का SI मात्रक कैंडेला है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Impulse","hi":"आवेग"},"2":{"en":"Velocity","hi":"वेग"},"3":{"en":"Magnetic permeability","hi":"चुंबकीय पारगम्यता"},"4":{"en":"Luminous intensity","hi":"ज्योति तीव्रता"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Luminous intensity</b><br>The <b>candela (cd)</b> is the SI base unit of <b><u>luminous intensity</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Seven SI base units: <b>metre, kilogram, second, ampere, kelvin, mole, candela</b>.<br>• <b>Impulse</b> – N·s; <b>Velocity</b> – m/s; <b>Permeability</b> – H/m.<br>• Luminous flux – <b>lumen</b>; illuminance – <b>lux</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – ज्योति तीव्रता</b><br><b>कैंडेला (cd)</b> <b><u>ज्योति तीव्रता (Luminous intensity)</u></b> का SI मूल मात्रक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सात SI मूल मात्रक: <b>मीटर, किलोग्राम, सेकंड, एम्पियर, केल्विन, मोल, कैंडेला</b>।<br>• <b>आवेग</b> – N·s; <b>वेग</b> – m/s; <b>पारगम्यता</b> – H/m।<br>• ज्योति फ्लक्स – <b>ल्यूमेन</b>; प्रदीप्ति – <b>लक्स</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000074112","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"<b>Fill in the blank:</b><br>The point on the Earth's surface vertically above the 'Focus' (Hypocentre) where an earthquake originates is called the _________. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>रिक्त स्थान भरिए:</b><br>पृथ्वी की सतह पर 'फोकस' (अवकेंद्र) के ठीक ऊपर स्थित बिंदु, जहाँ भूकंप उत्पन्न होता है, _________ कहलाता है। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Isocentre","hi":"आइसोसेंटर"},"2":{"en":"Epicenter","hi":"अधिकेंद्र"},"3":{"en":"Seismic Core","hi":"भूकंपीय कोर"},"4":{"en":"Fault Plane","hi":"भ्रंश तल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Epicenter</b><br>The point on the surface directly above the focus is the <b><u>epicentre</u></b>; it is the first place to feel the seismic waves and usually suffers the most damage.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Earthquake waves are recorded by a <b>seismograph</b>.<br>• <b>P-waves</b> are fastest and travel through solids and liquids; <b>S-waves</b> only through solids.<br>• Magnitude is measured on the <b>Richter scale</b>; intensity on the <b>Mercalli scale</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अधिकेंद्र</b><br>फोकस के ठीक ऊपर सतह पर स्थित बिंदु <b><u>अधिकेंद्र (Epicentre)</u></b> है; यहीं भूकंपीय तरंगें सबसे पहले पहुँचती हैं और प्रायः सर्वाधिक क्षति होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भूकंपीय तरंगें <b>सिस्मोग्राफ</b> द्वारा दर्ज की जाती हैं।<br>• <b>P-तरंगें</b> सबसे तेज़ और ठोस व द्रव दोनों में चलती हैं; <b>S-तरंगें</b> केवल ठोस में।<br>• परिमाण <b>रिक्टर पैमाने</b> पर, तीव्रता <b>मरकेली पैमाने</b> पर मापी जाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000074113","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which mineral is associated with Gangpur and Sundergarh in Odisha? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"ओडिशा के गंगपुर और सुंदरगढ़ से कौन-सा खनिज संबद्ध है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Coal","hi":"कोयला"},"2":{"en":"Petroleum","hi":"पेट्रोलियम"},"3":{"en":"Manganese","hi":"मैंगनीज़"},"4":{"en":"Bauxite","hi":"बॉक्साइट"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Manganese</b><br><b>Odisha</b> is the leading producer of <b><u>manganese</u></b>; major deposits lie in the <b>Gangpur</b> belt of <b>Sundargarh</b>, and in Keonjhar, Bonai and Koraput.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Manganese is used mainly in <b>steel making</b> (about 10 kg per tonne of steel).<br>• Other major manganese states: <b>Madhya Pradesh (Balaghat), Maharashtra, Karnataka</b>.<br>• Odisha is also the top producer of <b>iron ore, chromite and bauxite</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – मैंगनीज़</b><br><b>ओडिशा</b> <b><u>मैंगनीज़</u></b> का प्रमुख उत्पादक है; मुख्य निक्षेप <b>सुंदरगढ़</b> की <b>गंगपुर</b> पट्टी तथा क्योंझर, बोनाई और कोरापुट में हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मैंगनीज़ का मुख्य उपयोग <b>इस्पात निर्माण</b> में होता है (लगभग 10 kg प्रति टन इस्पात)।<br>• अन्य प्रमुख मैंगनीज़ राज्य: <b>मध्य प्रदेश (बालाघाट), महाराष्ट्र, कर्नाटक</b>।<br>• ओडिशा <b>लौह अयस्क, क्रोमाइट और बॉक्साइट</b> का भी शीर्ष उत्पादक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000074114","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Consider the following pairs of folk music traditions and their corresponding states:<br>1. Malushahi – Uttarakhand<br>2. Manganiyar – Rajasthan<br>Which of the pairs given above is/are <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"लोक संगीत परंपराओं और उनके संबंधित राज्यों के निम्नलिखित युग्मों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. मालूशाही – उत्तराखंड<br>2. मांगणियार – राजस्थान<br>ऊपर दिए गए युग्मों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है/हैं? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both 1 and 2</b><br><b>Malushahi</b> is a ballad (love story of Malushahi and Rajula) sung in Kumaon, <b>Uttarakhand</b>; the <b>Manganiyars</b> are hereditary folk musicians of the Thar desert, <b>Rajasthan</b>. Both are correct: <b><u>Both 1 and 2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Manganiyars play the <b>kamaicha</b> and <b>khartal</b>; <b>Langas</b> are another musician community of Rajasthan.<br>• Other Uttarakhand forms: <b>Jagar, Chhopati, Bajuband</b>.<br>• Famous Manganiyar singer: <b>Mame Khan</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1 और 2 दोनों</b><br><b>मालूशाही</b> कुमाऊँ, <b>उत्तराखंड</b> में गाई जाने वाली गाथा (मालूशाही और राजुला की प्रेमकथा) है; <b>मांगणियार</b> थार मरुस्थल, <b>राजस्थान</b> के वंशानुगत लोक संगीतकार हैं। दोनों सही हैं: <b><u>1 और 2 दोनों</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मांगणियार <b>कमायचा</b> और <b>खड़ताल</b> बजाते हैं; <b>लंगा</b> राजस्थान का एक अन्य संगीतकार समुदाय है।<br>• उत्तराखंड के अन्य रूप: <b>जागर, छोपती, बाजूबंद</b>।<br>• प्रसिद्ध मांगणियार गायक: <b>मामे खान</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000074115","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"The PM SHRI (Prime Minister's Schools for Rising India) scheme is primarily designed to achieve which of the following objectives? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पीएम श्री (प्राइम मिनिस्टर्स स्कूल्स फॉर राइज़िंग इंडिया) योजना मुख्य रूप से निम्नलिखित में से किस उद्देश्य को प्राप्त करने के लिए बनाई गई है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To provide free laptops to all school students in rural areas","hi":"ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों के सभी स्कूली छात्रों को मुफ्त लैपटॉप देना"},"2":{"en":"To develop and upgrade selected schools as model institutions showcasing NEP 2020","hi":"चयनित विद्यालयों को NEP 2020 प्रदर्शित करने वाले आदर्श संस्थानों के रूप में विकसित और उन्नत करना"},"3":{"en":"To privatize government schools through public-private partnerships","hi":"सार्वजनिक-निजी भागीदारी से सरकारी विद्यालयों का निजीकरण"},"4":{"en":"To focus only on higher education and university reforms","hi":"केवल उच्च शिक्षा और विश्वविद्यालय सुधारों पर ध्यान"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – To develop and upgrade selected schools as model institutions showcasing NEP 2020</b><br><b>PM SHRI</b> aims to <b><u>upgrade over 14,500 existing schools into model schools</u></b> that showcase the implementation of <b>NEP 2020</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Approved in <b>September 2022</b>; a centrally sponsored scheme of the <b>Ministry of Education</b>.<br>• Schools are run by Centre, States, UTs and local bodies, including <b>KVs and JNVs</b>.<br>• Focus on <b>green schools</b>, smart classrooms and experiential learning.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – चयनित विद्यालयों को NEP 2020 प्रदर्शित करने वाले आदर्श संस्थानों के रूप में विकसित और उन्नत करना</b><br><b>पीएम श्री</b> का उद्देश्य <b><u>14,500 से अधिक मौजूदा विद्यालयों को आदर्श विद्यालयों के रूप में उन्नत करना</u></b> है, जो <b>NEP 2020</b> के कार्यान्वयन को प्रदर्शित करें।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>सितंबर 2022</b> में स्वीकृत; <b>शिक्षा मंत्रालय</b> की केंद्र प्रायोजित योजना।<br>• इसमें केंद्र, राज्यों, UT और स्थानीय निकायों के विद्यालय, जिनमें <b>केवी और जेएनवी</b> भी शामिल हैं।<br>• <b>हरित विद्यालय</b>, स्मार्ट कक्षाएँ और अनुभवात्मक शिक्षा पर ध्यान।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000074116","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"Which factor most differentiates BRICS (Brazil, Russia, India, China, and South Africa) from the Non-Aligned Movement (NAM)? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-सा कारक ब्रिक्स (ब्राज़ील, रूस, भारत, चीन और दक्षिण अफ्रीका) को गुटनिरपेक्ष आंदोलन (NAM) से सबसे अधिक अलग करता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Representation of developing countries","hi":"विकासशील देशों का प्रतिनिधित्व"},"2":{"en":"Focus on economic cooperation among major emerging economies","hi":"प्रमुख उभरती अर्थव्यवस्थाओं के बीच आर्थिक सहयोग पर ध्यान"},"3":{"en":"Opposition to colonialism","hi":"उपनिवेशवाद का विरोध"},"4":{"en":"Demand for sovereignty","hi":"संप्रभुता की माँग"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Focus on economic cooperation among major emerging economies</b><br>NAM was a political movement of newly independent nations staying away from Cold War blocs. BRICS is a smaller grouping focused on <b><u>economic cooperation among major emerging economies</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• NAM's first summit: <b>Belgrade (1961)</b>; founders include <b>Nehru, Tito, Nasser, Sukarno, Nkrumah</b>.<br>• NAM has about <b>120 members</b>; BRICS expanded from 5 to 10+ members.<br>• BRICS has the <b>New Development Bank</b> (Shanghai).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – प्रमुख उभरती अर्थव्यवस्थाओं के बीच आर्थिक सहयोग पर ध्यान</b><br>NAM नव-स्वतंत्र राष्ट्रों का राजनीतिक आंदोलन था जो शीत युद्ध के गुटों से दूर रहे। ब्रिक्स <b><u>प्रमुख उभरती अर्थव्यवस्थाओं के बीच आर्थिक सहयोग</u></b> पर केंद्रित छोटा समूह है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NAM का पहला शिखर सम्मेलन: <b>बेलग्रेड (1961)</b>; संस्थापकों में <b>नेहरू, टीटो, नासिर, सुकर्णो, नक्रूमा</b>।<br>• NAM के लगभग <b>120 सदस्य</b> हैं; ब्रिक्स 5 से बढ़कर 10+ सदस्य हुआ।<br>• ब्रिक्स का <b>न्यू डेवलपमेंट बैंक</b> (शंघाई) है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000074117","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"The Chabahar project strengthens India’s ability to access Afghanistan primarily through: [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"चाबहार परियोजना मुख्य रूप से किसके माध्यम से भारत की अफ़गानिस्तान तक पहुँच को मज़बूत करती है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Arabian Sea–Iran–Afghanistan route","hi":"अरब सागर–ईरान–अफ़गानिस्तान मार्ग"},"2":{"en":"Indian Ocean–Oman–Afghanistan route","hi":"हिंद महासागर–ओमान–अफ़गानिस्तान मार्ग"},"3":{"en":"Caspian Sea–Iran–Afghanistan route","hi":"कैस्पियन सागर–ईरान–अफ़गानिस्तान मार्ग"},"4":{"en":"Persian Gulf–Iran–Afghanistan route","hi":"फ़ारस की खाड़ी–ईरान–अफ़गानिस्तान मार्ग"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Arabian Sea–Iran–Afghanistan route</b><br><b>Chabahar Port</b> lies on Iran's south-east coast on the <b>Gulf of Oman / Arabian Sea</b>. Goods go from Indian ports across the Arabian Sea to Chabahar and then by road/rail through Iran to Afghanistan – the <b><u>Arabian Sea–Iran–Afghanistan route</u></b>, bypassing Pakistan.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India operates the <b>Shahid Beheshti terminal</b> through <b>IPGL</b>; a 10-year agreement was signed in <b>May 2024</b>.<br>• Chabahar is linked to the <b>INSTC</b> (International North–South Transport Corridor).<br>• It is about <b>170 km</b> west of Pakistan's <b>Gwadar port</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अरब सागर–ईरान–अफ़गानिस्तान मार्ग</b><br><b>चाबहार बंदरगाह</b> ईरान के दक्षिण-पूर्वी तट पर <b>ओमान की खाड़ी / अरब सागर</b> पर स्थित है। माल भारतीय बंदरगाहों से अरब सागर पार कर चाबहार और फिर ईरान से सड़क/रेल द्वारा अफ़गानिस्तान जाता है – <b><u>अरब सागर–ईरान–अफ़गानिस्तान मार्ग</u></b>, जिससे पाकिस्तान को बायपास किया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत <b>IPGL</b> के माध्यम से <b>शाहिद बेहेश्ती टर्मिनल</b> संचालित करता है; <b>मई 2024</b> में 10 वर्षीय समझौता हुआ।<br>• चाबहार <b>INSTC</b> (अंतर्राष्ट्रीय उत्तर–दक्षिण परिवहन गलियारा) से जुड़ा है।<br>• यह पाकिस्तान के <b>ग्वादर बंदरगाह</b> से लगभग <b>170 km</b> पश्चिम में है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000074118","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"The state government creates a special court of judicial magistrates first class for cyber fraud cases in a city. Later, a regular judicial magistrate first class in the same area takes cognizance of a cyber fraud case and begins trial proceedings. Which of the following is legally correct under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"राज्य सरकार किसी शहर में साइबर धोखाधड़ी मामलों के लिए प्रथम श्रेणी न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट का विशेष न्यायालय बनाती है। बाद में उसी क्षेत्र का एक नियमित प्रथम श्रेणी न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट साइबर धोखाधड़ी के मामले का संज्ञान लेकर विचारण शुरू करता है। भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023 के तहत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विधिक रूप से सही है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The regular magistrate can proceed because all judicial magistrates have concurrent jurisdiction.","hi":"नियमित मजिस्ट्रेट आगे बढ़ सकता है क्योंकि सभी न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेटों का समवर्ती क्षेत्राधिकार है।"},"2":{"en":"The regular magistrate can proceed only with sessions judge approval.","hi":"नियमित मजिस्ट्रेट केवल सत्र न्यायाधीश की स्वीकृति से आगे बढ़ सकता है।"},"3":{"en":"The regular magistrate lacks jurisdiction if the case falls within the class assigned to the special court.","hi":"यदि मामला विशेष न्यायालय को सौंपे गए वर्ग में आता है तो नियमित मजिस्ट्रेट के पास क्षेत्राधिकार नहीं है।"},"4":{"en":"The Special Court can hear only appeals, not trials.","hi":"विशेष न्यायालय केवल अपीलें सुन सकता है, विचारण नहीं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The regular magistrate lacks jurisdiction if the case falls within the class assigned to the special court.</b><br>Under <b>Section 11 of BNSS</b>, when a Special Court of Judicial Magistrates is established for a particular class of cases in a local area, <b><u>no other Magistrate in that area shall have jurisdiction</u></b> over cases of that class.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Special Courts are set up by the <b>State Government in consultation with the High Court</b>.<br>• Old provision: <b>Section 11 of CrPC, 1973</b>.<br>• BNSS came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>, replacing the CrPC.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – यदि मामला विशेष न्यायालय को सौंपे गए वर्ग में आता है तो नियमित मजिस्ट्रेट के पास क्षेत्राधिकार नहीं है।</b><br><b>BNSS की धारा 11</b> के तहत जब किसी स्थानीय क्षेत्र में किसी विशेष वर्ग के मामलों के लिए न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेटों का विशेष न्यायालय स्थापित होता है, तो <b><u>उस क्षेत्र में किसी अन्य मजिस्ट्रेट को उस वर्ग के मामलों का क्षेत्राधिकार नहीं</u></b> होता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विशेष न्यायालय <b>राज्य सरकार द्वारा उच्च न्यायालय के परामर्श से</b> स्थापित किए जाते हैं।<br>• पुराना प्रावधान: <b>CrPC, 1973 की धारा 11</b>।<br>• BNSS <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से CrPC के स्थान पर लागू हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000074119","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who has been appointed as the new Managing Director (MD) of Indraprastha Gas Limited (IGL) in June 2026? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जून 2026 में इंद्रप्रस्थ गैस लिमिटेड (IGL) के नए प्रबंध निदेशक (MD) के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sanjay Kumar","hi":"संजय कुमार"},"2":{"en":"Kumar Shanker","hi":"कुमार शंकर"},"3":{"en":"Neelkanth Mishra","hi":"नीलकंठ मिश्रा"},"4":{"en":"Ajay Rajan","hi":"अजय राजन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Kumar Shanker</b><br><b><u>Kumar Shanker</u></b> was appointed <b>Managing Director of Indraprastha Gas Limited</b> in <b>June 2026</b>, succeeding <b>Kamal Kishore Chatiwal</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• IGL supplies <b>CNG and PNG</b> in Delhi-NCR; it is a joint venture of <b>GAIL and BPCL</b>.<br>• IGL was incorporated in <b>1998</b>.<br>• City gas distribution is regulated by <b>PNGRB</b> (Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कुमार शंकर</b><br><b><u>कुमार शंकर</u></b> को <b>जून 2026</b> में <b>कमल किशोर चटीवाल</b> के स्थान पर <b>इंद्रप्रस्थ गैस लिमिटेड</b> का प्रबंध निदेशक नियुक्त किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• IGL दिल्ली-NCR में <b>CNG और PNG</b> की आपूर्ति करती है; यह <b>GAIL और BPCL</b> का संयुक्त उपक्रम है।<br>• IGL की स्थापना <b>1998</b> में हुई।<br>• शहरी गैस वितरण का विनियमन <b>PNGRB</b> (पेट्रोलियम और प्राकृतिक गैस विनियामक बोर्ड) करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000074120","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian wrestler became the youngest-ever Olympic medallist from India by winning Bronze in the 57kg category at the Paris 2024 Olympics? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पेरिस 2024 ओलंपिक में 57 kg वर्ग में कांस्य जीतकर कौन-सा भारतीय पहलवान भारत का अब तक का सबसे कम उम्र का ओलंपिक पदक विजेता बना? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bajrang Punia","hi":"बजरंग पुनिया"},"2":{"en":"Ravi Kumar Dahiya","hi":"रवि कुमार दहिया"},"3":{"en":"Aman Sehrawat","hi":"अमन सहरावत"},"4":{"en":"Antim Panghal","hi":"अंतिम पंघाल"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Aman Sehrawat</b><br><b><u>Aman Sehrawat</u></b> won <b>bronze</b> in men's freestyle <b>57 kg</b> at Paris 2024 at the age of <b>21</b>, becoming India's youngest Olympic medallist.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It was India's only wrestling medal at Paris 2024.<br>• <b>Ravi Dahiya</b> won silver in 57 kg at <b>Tokyo 2020</b>; <b>Bajrang Punia</b> won bronze in 65 kg at Tokyo.<br>• India's first Olympic wrestling medal: <b>K.D. Jadhav</b> (bronze, Helsinki 1952).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अमन सहरावत</b><br><b><u>अमन सहरावत</u></b> ने पेरिस 2024 में पुरुष फ्रीस्टाइल <b>57 kg</b> में <b>21</b> वर्ष की आयु में <b>कांस्य</b> जीता और भारत के सबसे कम उम्र के ओलंपिक पदक विजेता बने।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह पेरिस 2024 में भारत का एकमात्र कुश्ती पदक था।<br>• <b>रवि दहिया</b> ने <b>टोक्यो 2020</b> में 57 kg में रजत और <b>बजरंग पुनिया</b> ने 65 kg में कांस्य जीता।<br>• भारत का पहला ओलंपिक कुश्ती पदक: <b>के.डी. जाधव</b> (कांस्य, हेलसिंकी 1952)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000074121","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Environmental Conventions","question":{"en":"Which Ramsar site in Uttar Pradesh was highlighted during World Wetlands Day 2026 for ecological and cultural significance? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"विश्व आर्द्रभूमि दिवस 2026 के दौरान उत्तर प्रदेश के किस रामसर स्थल को पारिस्थितिक और सांस्कृतिक महत्व के लिए रेखांकित किया गया? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nawabganj Bird Sanctuary","hi":"नवाबगंज पक्षी अभयारण्य"},"2":{"en":"Parvati Arga Bird Sanctuary","hi":"पार्वती अरगा पक्षी अभयारण्य"},"3":{"en":"Samaspur Bird Sanctuary","hi":"समसपुर पक्षी अभयारण्य"},"4":{"en":"Sandi Bird Sanctuary","hi":"सांडी पक्षी अभयारण्य"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Parvati Arga Bird Sanctuary</b><br><b><u>Parvati Arga Bird Sanctuary</u></b> in <b>Gonda district</b>, Uttar Pradesh, a Ramsar site known for its oxbow lakes and migratory birds, was highlighted on World Wetlands Day 2026, whose theme focused on wetlands and traditional knowledge/culture.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• World Wetlands Day is observed on <b>2 February</b>, marking the <b>Ramsar Convention (1971)</b> signed at Ramsar, Iran.<br>• Parvati Arga was notified as an <b>Eco-Sensitive Zone</b> in December 2025.<br>• Other UP Ramsar sites include <b>Nawabganj, Samaspur, Sandi, Saman, Sarsai Nawar, Haiderpur</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पार्वती अरगा पक्षी अभयारण्य</b><br>उत्तर प्रदेश के <b>गोंडा ज़िले</b> में स्थित <b><u>पार्वती अरगा पक्षी अभयारण्य</u></b>, जो गोखुर झीलों और प्रवासी पक्षियों के लिए प्रसिद्ध रामसर स्थल है, को विश्व आर्द्रभूमि दिवस 2026 पर रेखांकित किया गया, जिसका विषय आर्द्रभूमि और पारंपरिक ज्ञान/संस्कृति पर केंद्रित था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विश्व आर्द्रभूमि दिवस <b>2 फरवरी</b> को मनाया जाता है, जो रामसर, ईरान में हस्ताक्षरित <b>रामसर कन्वेंशन (1971)</b> की याद में है।<br>• पार्वती अरगा को दिसंबर 2025 में <b>पर्यावरण-संवेदी क्षेत्र</b> अधिसूचित किया गया।<br>• उत्तर प्रदेश के अन्य रामसर स्थल: <b>नवाबगंज, समसपुर, सांडी, समान, सरसई नावर, हैदरपुर</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000074122","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: National Income","question":{"en":"Which of the following statement regarding nominal and real GDP (Gross Domestic Product) is <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"नाममात्र और वास्तविक GDP (सकल घरेलू उत्पाद) के संबंध में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन <b>सही</b> है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Real GDP is calculated using current-year prices whereas nominal GDP uses base-year prices.","hi":"वास्तविक GDP चालू वर्ष की कीमतों पर और नाममात्र GDP आधार वर्ष की कीमतों पर गणना की जाती है।"},"2":{"en":"Real GDP and nominal GDP always remain equal in every accounting year.","hi":"वास्तविक GDP और नाममात्र GDP प्रत्येक लेखा वर्ष में सदैव समान रहते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Real GDP removes the effect of price changes through constant-base-year prices.","hi":"वास्तविक GDP स्थिर आधार-वर्ष कीमतों द्वारा कीमत परिवर्तनों के प्रभाव को हटा देता है।"},"4":{"en":"Real GDP excludes services while nominal GDP includes both goods and services.","hi":"वास्तविक GDP में सेवाएँ शामिल नहीं होतीं जबकि नाममात्र GDP में वस्तुएँ और सेवाएँ दोनों शामिल होती हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Real GDP removes the effect of price changes through constant-base-year prices.</b><br><b>Nominal GDP</b> is valued at current prices; <b>Real GDP</b> is valued at <b><u>constant (base-year) prices, removing the effect of price changes</u></b>, so it shows the real change in output.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• \\(\\text{GDP Deflator} = \\frac{\\text{Nominal GDP}}{\\text{Real GDP}} \\times 100\\).<br>• India's current base year for GDP is <b>2011–12</b> (being revised to <b>2022–23</b>).<br>• GDP is estimated in India by the <b>NSO (MoSPI)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – वास्तविक GDP स्थिर आधार-वर्ष कीमतों द्वारा कीमत परिवर्तनों के प्रभाव को हटा देता है।</b><br><b>नाममात्र GDP</b> चालू कीमतों पर आँका जाता है; <b>वास्तविक GDP</b> <b><u>स्थिर (आधार-वर्ष) कीमतों पर आँका जाता है, जिससे कीमत परिवर्तनों का प्रभाव हट जाता है</u></b>, अतः यह उत्पादन में वास्तविक परिवर्तन दर्शाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• \\(\\text{GDP Deflator} = \\frac{\\text{Nominal GDP}}{\\text{Real GDP}} \\times 100\\)।<br>• भारत में GDP का आधार वर्ष <b>2011–12</b> है (<b>2022–23</b> में संशोधित किया जा रहा है)।<br>• भारत में GDP का आकलन <b>NSO (MoSPI)</b> करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000074123","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a Maharatna Central Public Sector Enterprise? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा महारत्न केंद्रीय सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र उद्यम है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hindustan Aeronautics Limited","hi":"हिंदुस्तान एयरोनॉटिक्स लिमिटेड"},"2":{"en":"Mahanagar Telephone Nigam Limited","hi":"महानगर टेलीफोन निगम लिमिटेड"},"3":{"en":"Indian Oil Corporation Limited","hi":"इंडियन ऑयल कॉर्पोरेशन लिमिटेड"},"4":{"en":"Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited","hi":"भारत संचार निगम लिमिटेड"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Indian Oil Corporation Limited</b><br><b><u>Indian Oil Corporation Limited (IOCL)</u></b> was among the first CPSEs to get <b>Maharatna</b> status (2010). MTNL and BSNL are not Maharatnas.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Maharatna scheme was introduced in <b>2009</b>; first Maharatnas: <b>NTPC, ONGC, SAIL, IOCL</b>.<br>• Criteria include average annual net profit of over <b>₹5,000 crore</b> and turnover over <b>₹25,000 crore</b>.<br>• Maharatna boards can invest up to <b>₹5,000 crore</b> without government approval.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – इंडियन ऑयल कॉर्पोरेशन लिमिटेड</b><br><b><u>इंडियन ऑयल कॉर्पोरेशन लिमिटेड (IOCL)</u></b> <b>महारत्न</b> दर्जा (2010) पाने वाले पहले CPSE में से है। MTNL और BSNL महारत्न नहीं हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• महारत्न योजना <b>2009</b> में शुरू हुई; पहले महारत्न: <b>NTPC, ONGC, SAIL, IOCL</b>।<br>• मानदंडों में औसत वार्षिक शुद्ध लाभ <b>₹5,000 करोड़</b> से अधिक और कारोबार <b>₹25,000 करोड़</b> से अधिक शामिल है।<br>• महारत्न बोर्ड सरकारी स्वीकृति के बिना <b>₹5,000 करोड़</b> तक निवेश कर सकते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000074124","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Human Geography","question":{"en":"Which of the following population trends is most likely to occur in a region with a high birth rate and a rapidly declining death rate? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"उच्च जन्म दर और तेज़ी से घटती मृत्यु दर वाले क्षेत्र में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी जनसंख्या प्रवृत्ति होने की सर्वाधिक संभावना है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Population stagnation","hi":"जनसंख्या स्थिरता"},"2":{"en":"Negative growth","hi":"ऋणात्मक वृद्धि"},"3":{"en":"Population explosion","hi":"जनसंख्या विस्फोट"},"4":{"en":"Zero growth","hi":"शून्य वृद्धि"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Population explosion</b><br>When the birth rate stays high but the death rate falls sharply, the gap (natural increase) widens rapidly, causing a <b><u>population explosion</u></b> – the second stage of the demographic transition.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In India, <b>1951–1981</b> is called the period of <b>population explosion</b>.<br>• <b>1921</b> is the \"Year of Great Divide\" in Indian demography.<br>• Stage 3 of demographic transition: falling birth rate; Stage 4: low birth and death rates.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जनसंख्या विस्फोट</b><br>जब जन्म दर ऊँची रहती है परंतु मृत्यु दर तेज़ी से घटती है, तो दोनों का अंतर (प्राकृतिक वृद्धि) तेज़ी से बढ़ता है, जिससे <b><u>जनसंख्या विस्फोट</u></b> होता है – यह जनांकिकीय संक्रमण की दूसरी अवस्था है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में <b>1951–1981</b> को <b>जनसंख्या विस्फोट</b> की अवधि कहा जाता है।<br>• <b>1921</b> भारतीय जनांकिकी में \"महाविभाजन वर्ष\" है।<br>• जनांकिकीय संक्रमण की तीसरी अवस्था: घटती जन्म दर; चौथी अवस्था: निम्न जन्म और मृत्यु दर।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000074125","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the primary cause of the major breakdown and eventual failure of the Third Five-Year Plan to reach its targets? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"तीसरी पंचवर्षीय योजना के लक्ष्य प्राप्त न कर पाने और उसकी विफलता का मुख्य कारण निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Runaway international crude oil price spikes","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय कच्चे तेल की कीमतों में अनियंत्रित वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"External conflicts and severe droughts","hi":"बाहरी संघर्ष और गंभीर सूखा"},"3":{"en":"Political instability at the central government","hi":"केंद्र सरकार में राजनीतिक अस्थिरता"},"4":{"en":"Implementation of massive pay commission awards","hi":"बड़े वेतन आयोग पुरस्कारों का कार्यान्वयन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – External conflicts and severe droughts</b><br>The <b>Third Plan (1961–66)</b> failed mainly due to <b><u>wars with China (1962) and Pakistan (1965)</u></b> and the <b>severe drought of 1965–66</b>. It achieved only about 2.4% growth against a 5.6% target.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Third Plan was also called the <b>Gadgil Yojana</b>; aim: self-reliant and self-generating economy.<br>• Its failure led to <b>Plan Holidays (1966–69)</b> with three Annual Plans.<br>• The <b>Green Revolution</b> began during the Plan Holiday period.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बाहरी संघर्ष और गंभीर सूखा</b><br><b>तीसरी योजना (1961–66)</b> मुख्यतः <b><u>चीन (1962) और पाकिस्तान (1965) से युद्धों</u></b> तथा <b>1965–66 के गंभीर सूखे</b> के कारण विफल रही। इसने 5.6% लक्ष्य के मुकाबले केवल लगभग 2.4% वृद्धि प्राप्त की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• तीसरी योजना को <b>गाडगिल योजना</b> भी कहा जाता है; उद्देश्य: आत्मनिर्भर और स्व-उत्पादक अर्थव्यवस्था।<br>• इसकी विफलता के बाद <b>योजना अवकाश (1966–69)</b> में तीन वार्षिक योजनाएँ रहीं।<br>• <b>हरित क्रांति</b> योजना अवकाश के दौरान शुरू हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000074126","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which biological experiment was successfully demonstrated aboard the PSLV Orbital Experimental Module-04 (POEM-4)? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"PSLV कक्षीय प्रायोगिक मॉड्यूल-04 (POEM-4) पर कौन-सा जैविक प्रयोग सफलतापूर्वक प्रदर्शित किया गया? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Animal tissue regeneration","hi":"पशु ऊतक पुनर्जनन"},"2":{"en":"Seed germination in microgravity","hi":"सूक्ष्म-गुरुत्व में बीज अंकुरण"},"3":{"en":"Human cell culture growth","hi":"मानव कोशिका संवर्धन वृद्धि"},"4":{"en":"Plant pollination in orbit","hi":"कक्षा में पादप परागण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Seed germination in microgravity</b><br>ISRO's <b>CROPS</b> (Compact Research Module for Orbital Plant Studies) experiment on <b>POEM-4</b> (PSLV-C60, December 2024) achieved <b><u>germination of cowpea seeds in microgravity</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• CROPS was developed by <b>VSSC</b>; cowpea seeds sprouted within <b>4 days</b>.<br>• PSLV-C60 also launched the <b>SpaDeX</b> docking mission.<br>• POEM uses the spent <b>PS4 stage</b> of PSLV as an orbital platform.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सूक्ष्म-गुरुत्व में बीज अंकुरण</b><br><b>POEM-4</b> (PSLV-C60, दिसंबर 2024) पर ISRO के <b>CROPS</b> (कक्षीय पादप अध्ययन हेतु कॉम्पैक्ट अनुसंधान मॉड्यूल) प्रयोग में <b><u>सूक्ष्म-गुरुत्व में लोबिया (Cowpea) के बीजों का अंकुरण</u></b> सफल रहा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• CROPS को <b>VSSC</b> ने विकसित किया; लोबिया के बीज <b>4 दिनों</b> में अंकुरित हुए।<br>• PSLV-C60 ने <b>SpaDeX</b> डॉकिंग मिशन भी प्रक्षेपित किया।<br>• POEM, PSLV के प्रयुक्त <b>PS4 चरण</b> को कक्षीय मंच के रूप में उपयोग करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000074127","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"A prey population increases from 400 individuals to 600 individuals over one year. What is the percentage growth in the population during this period? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक शिकार जनसंख्या एक वर्ष में 400 से बढ़कर 600 हो जाती है। इस अवधि में जनसंख्या में प्रतिशत वृद्धि कितनी है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25%"},"2":{"en":"33%"},"3":{"en":"60%"},"4":{"en":"50%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – 50%</b><br>Increase = 600 − 400 = 200<br>Percentage growth = \\(\\frac{200}{400} \\times 100 = 50\\%\\) = <b><u>50%</u></b><br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Population growth depends on <b>natality, mortality, immigration and emigration</b>.<br>• Unlimited resources give <b>exponential (J-shaped)</b> growth; limited resources give <b>logistic (S-shaped)</b> growth.<br>• The maximum population an environment can support is its <b>carrying capacity (K)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – 50%</b><br>वृद्धि = 600 − 400 = 200<br>प्रतिशत वृद्धि = \\(\\frac{200}{400} \\times 100 = 50\\%\\) = <b><u>50%</u></b><br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जनसंख्या वृद्धि <b>जन्म दर, मृत्यु दर, आप्रवास और उत्प्रवास</b> पर निर्भर करती है।<br>• असीमित संसाधनों में <b>चरघातांकी (J-आकार)</b> वृद्धि; सीमित संसाधनों में <b>लॉजिस्टिक (S-आकार)</b> वृद्धि होती है।<br>• पर्यावरण द्वारा पोषित अधिकतम जनसंख्या उसकी <b>वहन क्षमता (K)</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000074128","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Diseases","question":{"en":"An antibody titre increases from 1:20 before vaccination to 1:320 after vaccination. By what factor has the antibody titre increased? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"टीकाकरण से पहले एक प्रतिरक्षी अनुमापांक 1:20 से बढ़कर टीकाकरण के बाद 1:320 हो जाता है। प्रतिरक्षी अनुमापांक किस गुणक से बढ़ा है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"16-fold","hi":"16 गुना"},"2":{"en":"12-fold","hi":"12 गुना"},"3":{"en":"19-fold","hi":"19 गुना"},"4":{"en":"20-fold","hi":"20 गुना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 16-fold</b><br>Fold increase = \\(\\frac{320}{20} = 16\\)<br>The antibody titre has increased <b><u>16-fold</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Antibody titre is the <b>highest dilution</b> of serum that still shows a positive reaction.<br>• A <b>four-fold or greater</b> rise is usually taken as a significant immune response.<br>• Antibodies are produced by <b>B-lymphocytes (plasma cells)</b>; the most abundant is <b>IgG</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 16 गुना</b><br>गुना वृद्धि = \\(\\frac{320}{20} = 16\\)<br>प्रतिरक्षी अनुमापांक <b><u>16 गुना</u></b> बढ़ा है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रतिरक्षी अनुमापांक सीरम का वह <b>उच्चतम तनुकरण</b> है जो अभी भी सकारात्मक प्रतिक्रिया दिखाता है।<br>• <b>चार गुना या अधिक</b> वृद्धि को सामान्यतः महत्वपूर्ण प्रतिरक्षा प्रतिक्रिया माना जाता है।<br>• प्रतिरक्षी <b>B-लसीकाणुओं (प्लाज़्मा कोशिकाएँ)</b> द्वारा बनते हैं; सबसे प्रचुर <b>IgG</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000074129","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Who chaired the Punjab and Bengal Boundary Commissions that demarcated the borders between India and Pakistan? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत और पाकिस्तान के बीच सीमाओं का निर्धारण करने वाले पंजाब और बंगाल सीमा आयोगों की अध्यक्षता किसने की? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lord Wavell","hi":"लॉर्ड वेवेल"},"2":{"en":"Sir Stafford Cripps","hi":"सर स्टैफ़र्ड क्रिप्स"},"3":{"en":"Lord Mountbatten","hi":"लॉर्ड माउंटबेटन"},"4":{"en":"Sir Cyril Radcliffe","hi":"सर सिरिल रैडक्लिफ़"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Sir Cyril Radcliffe</b><br><b><u>Sir Cyril Radcliffe</u></b> chaired both the Punjab and Bengal Boundary Commissions; the boundary is called the <b>Radcliffe Line</b>, announced on <b>17 August 1947</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Radcliffe had never visited India before and completed the task in about <b>five weeks</b>.<br>• <b>Stafford Cripps</b> led the Cripps Mission (1942); <b>Wavell</b> – Shimla Conference (1945).<br>• <b>Durand Line</b> – Afghanistan–Pakistan; <b>McMahon Line</b> – India–China.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – सर सिरिल रैडक्लिफ़</b><br><b><u>सर सिरिल रैडक्लिफ़</u></b> ने पंजाब और बंगाल दोनों सीमा आयोगों की अध्यक्षता की; इस सीमा को <b>रैडक्लिफ़ रेखा</b> कहते हैं, जिसकी घोषणा <b>17 अगस्त 1947</b> को हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• रैडक्लिफ़ पहले कभी भारत नहीं आए थे और उन्होंने लगभग <b>पाँच सप्ताह</b> में यह कार्य पूरा किया।<br>• <b>स्टैफ़र्ड क्रिप्स</b> – क्रिप्स मिशन (1942); <b>वेवेल</b> – शिमला सम्मेलन (1945)।<br>• <b>डूरंड रेखा</b> – अफ़गानिस्तान–पाकिस्तान; <b>मैकमोहन रेखा</b> – भारत–चीन।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000074130","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following plans formed the immediate basis of the Indian Independence Act, 1947? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी योजना भारतीय स्वतंत्रता अधिनियम, 1947 का तात्कालिक आधार बनी? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Wavell Plan","hi":"वेवेल योजना"},"2":{"en":"Cripps Proposal","hi":"क्रिप्स प्रस्ताव"},"3":{"en":"Mountbatten Plan","hi":"माउंटबेटन योजना"},"4":{"en":"August Offer","hi":"अगस्त प्रस्ताव"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Mountbatten Plan</b><br>The <b><u>Mountbatten Plan</u></b> (3 June Plan, 1947) proposed partition into two dominions, India and Pakistan; it was given legal form by the <b>Indian Independence Act, 1947</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Act received royal assent on <b>18 July 1947</b>.<br>• <b>August Offer</b> – 1940 (Linlithgow); <b>Cripps Proposal</b> – 1942; <b>Wavell Plan</b> – 1945.<br>• Mountbatten was the <b>last Viceroy</b> and the first Governor-General of independent India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – माउंटबेटन योजना</b><br><b><u>माउंटबेटन योजना</u></b> (3 जून योजना, 1947) ने भारत और पाकिस्तान दो डोमिनियनों में विभाजन का प्रस्ताव रखा; इसे <b>भारतीय स्वतंत्रता अधिनियम, 1947</b> द्वारा कानूनी रूप दिया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अधिनियम को <b>18 जुलाई 1947</b> को शाही स्वीकृति मिली।<br>• <b>अगस्त प्रस्ताव</b> – 1940 (लिनलिथगो); <b>क्रिप्स प्रस्ताव</b> – 1942; <b>वेवेल योजना</b> – 1945।<br>• माउंटबेटन <b>अंतिम वायसराय</b> और स्वतंत्र भारत के पहले गवर्नर-जनरल थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000074131","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{x}{256}} = \\frac{17}{16}\\), find the value of x. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{x}{256}} = \\frac{17}{16}\\) है, तो x का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"24"},"2":{"en":"45"},"3":{"en":"52"},"4":{"en":"33"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Squaring: \\(1 + \\frac{x}{256} = \\frac{289}{256}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x}{256} = \\frac{289 - 256}{256} = \\frac{33}{256}\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{33}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 33.</b>","hi":"वर्ग करने पर: \\(1 + \\frac{x}{256} = \\frac{289}{256}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x}{256} = \\frac{289 - 256}{256} = \\frac{33}{256}\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{33}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 33 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000074132","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify: [(0.6)⁴ − (0.5)⁴] ÷ [(0.6)² + (0.5)²]. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सरलीकृत कीजिए: [(0.6)⁴ − (0.5)⁴] ÷ [(0.6)² + (0.5)²]। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.15"},"2":{"en":"0.11"},"3":{"en":"0.18"},"4":{"en":"0.19"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(a^4 - b^4 = (a^2 - b^2)(a^2 + b^2)\\), so the expression reduces to \\(a^2 - b^2\\)<br>\\(= 0.36 - 0.25\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{0.11}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.11.</b>","hi":"\\(a^4 - b^4 = (a^2 - b^2)(a^2 + b^2)\\), अतः व्यंजक \\(a^2 - b^2\\) बन जाता है<br>\\(= 0.36 - 0.25\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{0.11}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0.11 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000074133","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"If A : B = 5 : 6 and B : C = 10 : 9, find A : B : C. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि A : B = 5 : 6 और B : C = 10 : 9 है, तो A : B : C ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25:30:27"},"2":{"en":"15:20:9"},"3":{"en":"10:15:17"},"4":{"en":"25:40:19"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Make B common: \\(A : B = 5 : 6 = 25 : 30\\) and \\(B : C = 10 : 9 = 30 : 27\\)<br>\\(A : B : C = \\boxed{25 : 30 : 27}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 25:30:27.</b>","hi":"B को समान कीजिए: \\(A : B = 5 : 6 = 25 : 30\\) और \\(B : C = 10 : 9 = 30 : 27\\)<br>\\(A : B : C = \\boxed{25 : 30 : 27}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 25:30:27 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000074134","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A alone completes a work in 12 days. With the help of an assistant, the work is completed in 8 days. If total wages are ₹600, find the assistant's share. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"A अकेले किसी कार्य को 12 दिनों में पूरा करता है। एक सहायक की मदद से कार्य 8 दिनों में पूरा हो जाता है। यदि कुल मज़दूरी ₹600 है, तो सहायक का हिस्सा ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹260"},"2":{"en":"₹140"},"3":{"en":"₹160"},"4":{"en":"₹200"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(A = \\frac{1}{12}\\), together \\(= \\frac{1}{8}\\), so assistant \\(= \\frac{1}{8} - \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{1}{24}\\)<br>Work ratio \\(A : \\) assistant \\(= \\frac{1}{12} : \\frac{1}{24} = 2 : 1\\)<br>Assistant's share ₹\\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 600 = \\boxed{200}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹200.</b>","hi":"\\(A = \\frac{1}{12}\\), मिलकर \\(= \\frac{1}{8}\\), अतः सहायक \\(= \\frac{1}{8} - \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{1}{24}\\)<br>कार्य अनुपात \\(A : \\) सहायक \\(= \\frac{1}{12} : \\frac{1}{24} = 2 : 1\\)<br>सहायक का हिस्सा ₹\\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 600 = \\boxed{200}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹200 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000074135","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 4\\sqrt{2}\\), then find the value of \\(x^4 + \\frac{1}{x^4}\\). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 4\\sqrt{2}\\) है, तो \\(x^4 + \\frac{1}{x^4}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"884"},"2":{"en":"878"},"3":{"en":"898"},"4":{"en":"866"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = (4\\sqrt{2})^2 - 2 = 32 - 2 = 30\\)<br>\\(x^4 + \\frac{1}{x^4} = 30^2 - 2 = 900 - 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{898}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 898.</b>","hi":"\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = (4\\sqrt{2})^2 - 2 = 32 - 2 = 30\\)<br>\\(x^4 + \\frac{1}{x^4} = 30^2 - 2 = 900 - 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{898}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 898 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000074136","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A person divided a sum of ₹17,200 into two parts and invested them at 8% and 10% per annum simple interest respectively. If the total interest received after 2 years is ₹3,008, what is the difference between the two parts? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति ने ₹17,200 की राशि को दो भागों में बाँटकर क्रमशः 8% और 10% प्रति वर्ष साधारण ब्याज पर निवेश किया। यदि 2 वर्षों बाद प्राप्त कुल ब्याज ₹3,008 है, तो दोनों भागों का अंतर क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹4,000"},"2":{"en":"₹4,400"},"3":{"en":"₹5,200"},"4":{"en":"₹3,600"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Effective 2-year rates: 16% and 20%<br>\\(0.16x + 0.20(17{,}200 - x) = 3008 \\Rightarrow 3440 - 0.04x = 3008\\)<br>\\(0.04x = 432 \\Rightarrow x = 10{,}800\\); other part \\(= 6400\\)<br>Difference ₹\\(= \\boxed{4{,}400}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹4,400.</b>","hi":"2 वर्ष की प्रभावी दरें: 16% और 20%<br>\\(0.16x + 0.20(17{,}200 - x) = 3008 \\Rightarrow 3440 - 0.04x = 3008\\)<br>\\(0.04x = 432 \\Rightarrow x = 10{,}800\\); दूसरा भाग \\(= 6400\\)<br>अंतर ₹\\(= \\boxed{4{,}400}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹4,400 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000074137","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"The graph of the equation 2x + 0y = 10 represents a: [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"समीकरण 2x + 0y = 10 का ग्राफ दर्शाता है: [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Horizontal line at y = 5","hi":"y = 5 पर क्षैतिज रेखा"},"2":{"en":"Vertical line at x = 5","hi":"x = 5 पर ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखा"},"3":{"en":"Line passing through the origin","hi":"मूल बिंदु से गुजरने वाली रेखा"},"4":{"en":"Oblique line","hi":"तिर्यक रेखा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(2x + 0y = 10 \\Rightarrow x = 5\\) for every value of y<br>So the graph is the vertical line \\(\\boxed{x = 5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Vertical line at x = 5.</b>","hi":"\\(2x + 0y = 10 \\Rightarrow x = 5\\) y के प्रत्येक मान के लिए<br>अतः ग्राफ ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखा \\(\\boxed{x = 5}\\) है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): x = 5 पर ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000074138","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A man deposits ₹2,00,000 at 10% p.a. compound interest. After the first year's interest is credited, he withdraws 40% of the interest earned. Find the balance at the end of the second year. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति ₹2,00,000, 10% प्रति वर्ष चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर जमा करता है। पहले वर्ष का ब्याज जमा होने के बाद वह अर्जित ब्याज का 40% निकाल लेता है। दूसरे वर्ष के अंत में शेष राशि ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹2,93,200"},"2":{"en":"₹2,63,200"},"3":{"en":"₹2,33,200"},"4":{"en":"₹2,03,200"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Year 1 interest \\(= 20{,}000\\); he withdraws 40% \\(= 8000\\)<br>Balance \\(= 2{,}20{,}000 - 8000 = 2{,}12{,}000\\)<br>Year 2 interest \\(= 21{,}200\\)<br>Balance ₹\\(= 2{,}12{,}000 + 21{,}200 = \\boxed{2{,}33{,}200}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹2,33,200.</b>","hi":"पहले वर्ष का ब्याज \\(= 20{,}000\\); वह 40% \\(= 8000\\) निकाल लेता है<br>शेष \\(= 2{,}20{,}000 - 8000 = 2{,}12{,}000\\)<br>दूसरे वर्ष का ब्याज \\(= 21{,}200\\)<br>शेष राशि ₹\\(= 2{,}12{,}000 + 21{,}200 = \\boxed{2{,}33{,}200}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹2,33,200 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000074139","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A box is 80 cm × 64 cm × 48 cm. Find how many cubes of side 8 cm can be arranged inside without gaps. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बॉक्स 80 cm × 64 cm × 48 cm है। इसमें बिना खाली जगह के 8 cm भुजा वाले कितने घन रखे जा सकते हैं? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"480"},"2":{"en":"370"},"3":{"en":"530"},"4":{"en":"250"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{80}{8} \\times \\frac{64}{8} \\times \\frac{48}{8} = 10 \\times 8 \\times 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{480}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 480.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{80}{8} \\times \\frac{64}{8} \\times \\frac{48}{8} = 10 \\times 8 \\times 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{480}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 480 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000074140","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord of a circle is 25.4 cm long. Determine the radius of the circle. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वृत्त की जीवा 25.4 cm लंबी है। वृत्त की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(r \\ge 12.7\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(r \\le 12.7\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"\\(r > 12.7\\) cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(r = 12.7\\) cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A chord is never longer than the diameter, so diameter \\(\\ge 25.4\\)<br>\\(r \\ge \\frac{25.4}{2} = 12.7\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{r \\ge 12.7\\ \\text{cm}}\\) (equality when the chord is a diameter)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(r \\ge 12.7\\) cm.</b>","hi":"जीवा व्यास से बड़ी नहीं हो सकती, अतः व्यास \\(\\ge 25.4\\)<br>\\(r \\ge \\frac{25.4}{2} = 12.7\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{r \\ge 12.7\\ \\text{cm}}\\) (समता तब जब जीवा व्यास हो)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(r \\ge 12.7\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000074141","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The area of a rhombus is 150 cm². If the ratio of its diagonals is 3:4, find its perimeter. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक समचतुर्भुज का क्षेत्रफल 150 cm² है। यदि उसके विकर्णों का अनुपात 3:4 है, तो उसका परिमाप ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40 cm"},"2":{"en":"50 cm"},"3":{"en":"60 cm"},"4":{"en":"80 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}(3x)(4x) = 6x^2 = 150 \\Rightarrow x^2 = 25 \\Rightarrow x = 5\\)<br>Diagonals \\(= 15\\) and \\(20\\), half-diagonals 7.5 and 10<br>Side \\(= \\sqrt{7.5^2 + 10^2} = 12.5\\) cm<br>Perimeter \\(= 4 \\times 12.5 = \\boxed{50\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 50 cm.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}(3x)(4x) = 6x^2 = 150 \\Rightarrow x^2 = 25 \\Rightarrow x = 5\\)<br>विकर्ण \\(= 15\\) और \\(20\\), अर्ध-विकर्ण 7.5 और 10<br>भुजा \\(= \\sqrt{7.5^2 + 10^2} = 12.5\\) cm<br>परिमाप \\(= 4 \\times 12.5 = \\boxed{50\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 50 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000074142","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"In a triangle ABC, right-angled at B, if \\(\\tan A = \\frac{5}{2}\\), find the value of \\(\\frac{\\sin A(\\cos C + \\cos A)}{\\cos C(\\sin C - \\sin A)}\\). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, B पर समकोण है, यदि \\(\\tan A = \\frac{5}{2}\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{\\sin A(\\cos C + \\cos A)}{\\cos C(\\sin C - \\sin A)}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{7}{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(-\\frac{7}{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(-\\frac{5}{2}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan A = \\frac{5}{2}\\) with \\(\\angle B = 90°\\), so \\(\\angle A + \\angle C = 90°\\): \\(\\cos C = \\sin A\\), \\(\\sin C = \\cos A\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{\\sin A(\\sin A + \\cos A)}{\\sin A(\\cos A - \\sin A)} = \\frac{\\sin A + \\cos A}{\\cos A - \\sin A}\\)<br>Divide by \\(\\cos A\\): \\(= \\frac{\\tan A + 1}{1 - \\tan A} = \\frac{2.5 + 1}{1 - 2.5} = \\frac{3.5}{-1.5}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-\\frac{7}{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(-\\frac{7}{3}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan A = \\frac{5}{2}\\) और \\(\\angle B = 90°\\), अतः \\(\\angle A + \\angle C = 90°\\): \\(\\cos C = \\sin A\\), \\(\\sin C = \\cos A\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{\\sin A(\\sin A + \\cos A)}{\\sin A(\\cos A - \\sin A)} = \\frac{\\sin A + \\cos A}{\\cos A - \\sin A}\\)<br>\\(\\cos A\\) से भाग देने पर: \\(= \\frac{\\tan A + 1}{1 - \\tan A} = \\frac{2.5 + 1}{1 - 2.5} = \\frac{3.5}{-1.5}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-\\frac{7}{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(-\\frac{7}{3}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000074143","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The base of a prism is a right-angled isosceles triangle whose hypotenuse is \\(4\\sqrt{2}\\) cm. If the height of the prism is 15 cm, find the volume of the prism. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक प्रिज़्म का आधार समकोण समद्विबाहु त्रिभुज है जिसका कर्ण \\(4\\sqrt{2}\\) cm है। यदि प्रिज़्म की ऊँचाई 15 cm है, तो प्रिज़्म का आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"120 cm³"},"2":{"en":"144 cm³"},"3":{"en":"96 cm³"},"4":{"en":"112 cm³"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Legs: \\(a\\sqrt{2} = 4\\sqrt{2} \\Rightarrow a = 4\\)<br>Base area \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4 \\times 4 = 8\\) cm²<br>Volume \\(= 8 \\times 15 = \\boxed{120\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 120 cm³.</b>","hi":"भुजाएँ: \\(a\\sqrt{2} = 4\\sqrt{2} \\Rightarrow a = 4\\)<br>आधार क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4 \\times 4 = 8\\) cm²<br>आयतन \\(= 8 \\times 15 = \\boxed{120\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 120 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000074144","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x = \\sqrt{\\frac{6 + \\sqrt{35}}{6 - \\sqrt{35}}}\\), then what is the value of \\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\)? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \\(x = \\sqrt{\\frac{6 + \\sqrt{35}}{6 - \\sqrt{35}}}\\) है, तो \\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"75"},"2":{"en":"86"},"3":{"en":"121"},"4":{"en":"142"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(x^2 = \\frac{6 + \\sqrt{35}}{6 - \\sqrt{35}}\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{x^2} = \\frac{6 - \\sqrt{35}}{6 + \\sqrt{35}}\\)<br>These are reciprocals, so put \\(y = x^2\\): \\(y + \\frac{1}{y} = \\frac{(6 + \\sqrt{35})^2 + (6 - \\sqrt{35})^2}{36 - 35}\\)<br>\\(= 2(36 + 35) = 142\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{142}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 142.</b>","hi":"\\(x^2 = \\frac{6 + \\sqrt{35}}{6 - \\sqrt{35}}\\) और \\(\\frac{1}{x^2} = \\frac{6 - \\sqrt{35}}{6 + \\sqrt{35}}\\)<br>ये परस्पर व्युत्क्रम हैं, \\(y = x^2\\) रखिए: \\(y + \\frac{1}{y} = \\frac{(6 + \\sqrt{35})^2 + (6 - \\sqrt{35})^2}{36 - 35}\\)<br>\\(= 2(36 + 35) = 142\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{142}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 142 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000074145","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two triangles, ABC and PQR, are congruent right-angled triangles where angle A and angle P are each 90°. If the hypotenuse BC measures 13 cm and side PR measures 5 cm, determine the length of side AB. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो त्रिभुज ABC और PQR सर्वांगसम समकोण त्रिभुज हैं जिनमें कोण A और कोण P प्रत्येक 90° हैं। यदि कर्ण BC = 13 cm और भुजा PR = 5 cm है, तो भुजा AB की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 cm"},"2":{"en":"6 cm"},"3":{"en":"12 cm"},"4":{"en":"10 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(PR\\) corresponds to \\(AC = 5\\) cm (congruent triangles)<br>\\(AB = \\sqrt{BC^2 - AC^2} = \\sqrt{169 - 25}\\)<br>\\(AB = \\sqrt{144} = \\boxed{12\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12 cm.</b>","hi":"\\(PR\\), \\(AC = 5\\) cm के संगत है (सर्वांगसम त्रिभुज)<br>\\(AB = \\sqrt{BC^2 - AC^2} = \\sqrt{169 - 25}\\)<br>\\(AB = \\sqrt{144} = \\boxed{12\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000074146","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord of a circle measures 40 cm and is 15 cm away from the centre. What will be the length of another chord of the same circle that is 20 cm away from the centre? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वृत्त की जीवा 40 cm है और केंद्र से 15 cm दूर है। उसी वृत्त की दूसरी जीवा, जो केंद्र से 20 cm दूर है, की लंबाई क्या होगी? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15 cm"},"2":{"en":"30 cm"},"3":{"en":"45 cm"},"4":{"en":"60 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(r^2 = 20^2 + 15^2 = 625 \\Rightarrow r = 25\\) cm<br>Other chord: half length \\(= \\sqrt{25^2 - 20^2} = 15\\) cm<br>Length \\(= 2 \\times 15 = \\boxed{30\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 30 cm.</b>","hi":"\\(r^2 = 20^2 + 15^2 = 625 \\Rightarrow r = 25\\) cm<br>दूसरी जीवा: आधी लंबाई \\(= \\sqrt{25^2 - 20^2} = 15\\) cm<br>लंबाई \\(= 2 \\times 15 = \\boxed{30\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 30 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000074147","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"An alloy contains 35% copper, 25% zinc and 40% nickel. How much copper (in kg) should be added to 20 kg of the alloy so that the new alloy contains 50% copper? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक मिश्रातु में 35% ताँबा, 25% जस्ता और 40% निकल है। 20 kg मिश्रातु में कितना ताँबा (kg में) मिलाया जाए कि नई मिश्रातु में 50% ताँबा हो जाए? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 kg"},"2":{"en":"6 kg"},"3":{"en":"12 kg"},"4":{"en":"16 kg"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Copper in 20 kg \\(= 7\\) kg<br>\\(\\frac{7 + x}{20 + x} = \\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow 14 + 2x = 20 + x\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{6\\ \\text{kg}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 6 kg.</b>","hi":"20 kg में ताँबा \\(= 7\\) kg<br>\\(\\frac{7 + x}{20 + x} = \\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow 14 + 2x = 20 + x\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{6\\ \\text{kg}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 6 kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000074148","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Read the following frequency polygon which represents class interval (Axis Daily Traffic Volume (Hundreds of Unique Users)) on the x-axis and frequency (Number of Days) on the y-axis, and answer the following question:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019e599f-2bfc-7195-b34c-541d470b5872_EN.jpg?edu=639294371652450330\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Which interval shows the sharpest decline in number of days compared to the previous interval? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित आवृत्ति बहुभुज पढ़िए जिसमें x-अक्ष पर वर्ग अंतराल (दैनिक ट्रैफिक वॉल्यूम, सैकड़ों में) और y-अक्ष पर आवृत्ति (दिनों की संख्या) है, और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019e599f-2bfc-7195-b34c-541d470b5872_HI.jpg?edu=639294371775365198\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>कौन-सा अंतराल पिछले अंतराल की तुलना में दिनों की संख्या में सबसे तेज़ गिरावट दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"70–90 to 90–110","hi":"70–90 से 90–110"},"2":{"en":"110–130 to 130–150","hi":"110–130 से 130–150"},"3":{"en":"90–110 to 110–130","hi":"90–110 से 110–130"},"4":{"en":"130–150 to 150–170","hi":"130–150 से 150–170"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Reading the polygon: 30–50 → 0, 50–70 → 40, 70–90 → 110, 90–110 → 72, 110–130 → 30, 130–150 → 15, 150–170 → 0<br>Fall after 70–90: \\(110 - 72 = 38\\); after 90–110: \\(72 - 30 = 42\\)<br>Sharpest decline \\(= \\boxed{90-110\\ \\text{to}\\ 110-130}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 90–110 to 110–130.</b>","hi":"बहुभुज पढ़ने पर: 30–50 → 0, 50–70 → 40, 70–90 → 110, 90–110 → 72, 110–130 → 30, 130–150 → 15, 150–170 → 0<br>70–90 के बाद गिरावट: \\(110 - 72 = 38\\); 90–110 के बाद: \\(72 - 30 = 42\\)<br>सबसे तेज़ गिरावट \\(= \\boxed{90-110\\ \\text{से}\\ 110-130}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 90–110 से 110–130 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019e599f-2bfc-7195-b34c-541d470b5872_EN.jpg?edu=639294371652450330","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019e599f-2bfc-7195-b34c-541d470b5872_HI.jpg?edu=639294371775365198"]}},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000074149","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The radius of a cylinder is increased by 25% and its height is decreased by 20%. Find the percentage change in its volume. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बेलन की त्रिज्या 25% बढ़ाई जाती है और ऊँचाई 20% घटाई जाती है। उसके आयतन में प्रतिशत परिवर्तन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15% decrease","hi":"15% कमी"},"2":{"en":"25% increase","hi":"25% वृद्धि"},"3":{"en":"10% increase","hi":"10% वृद्धि"},"4":{"en":"20% decrease","hi":"20% कमी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(V \\propto r^2h\\)<br>Factor \\(= (1.25)^2 \\times 0.8 = 1.5625 \\times 0.8 = 1.25\\)<br>Change \\(= \\boxed{25\\%\\ \\text{increase}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 25% increase.</b>","hi":"\\(V \\propto r^2h\\)<br>गुणक \\(= (1.25)^2 \\times 0.8 = 1.5625 \\times 0.8 = 1.25\\)<br>परिवर्तन \\(= \\boxed{25\\%\\ \\text{वृद्धि}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 25% वृद्धि है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000074150","section":"MATH","topic":"Discount","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper marks an article 35% above its cost price. If he sells it after allowing a discount of 15%, what is his gain percentage? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक दुकानदार किसी वस्तु को उसके क्रय मूल्य से 35% अधिक अंकित करता है। यदि वह 15% छूट देकर उसे बेचता है, तो उसका लाभ प्रतिशत क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18.35%"},"2":{"en":"16.25%"},"3":{"en":"14.75%"},"4":{"en":"19.55%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let CP \\(= 100\\), MP \\(= 135\\)<br>SP \\(= 135 \\times 0.85 = 114.75\\)<br>Gain \\(= \\boxed{14.75\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 14.75%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए क्रय मूल्य \\(= 100\\), अंकित मूल्य \\(= 135\\)<br>विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 135 \\times 0.85 = 114.75\\)<br>लाभ \\(= \\boxed{14.75\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 14.75% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000074151","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Read the given histogram carefully which shows daily wages (in ₹) of workers along with the number of workers (frequency) in each class interval and answer the question that follows:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019e69ce-f74a-74e0-a197-9f7d34c846c3_EN.jpg?edu=639294371653349927\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Determine the median class of wages. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिए गए आयतचित्र को ध्यान से पढ़िए जो श्रमिकों की दैनिक मज़दूरी (₹ में) तथा प्रत्येक वर्ग अंतराल में श्रमिकों की संख्या (आवृत्ति) दर्शाता है, और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019e69ce-f74a-74e0-a197-9f7d34c846c3_HI.jpg?edu=639294371776042170\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>मज़दूरी का माध्यक वर्ग ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"190–200"},"2":{"en":"200–210"},"3":{"en":"170–180"},"4":{"en":"180–190"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Frequencies: 55, 80, 108, 117, 150, 105, 70 → total \\(N = 585\\), so \\(\\frac{N}{2} = 292.5\\)<br>Cumulative: 55, 135, 243, 360 …<br>292.5 is first crossed in the class 180–190<br>Median class \\(= \\boxed{180-190}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 180–190.</b>","hi":"आवृत्तियाँ: 55, 80, 108, 117, 150, 105, 70 → कुल \\(N = 585\\), अतः \\(\\frac{N}{2} = 292.5\\)<br>संचयी: 55, 135, 243, 360 …<br>292.5 पहली बार 180–190 वर्ग में पार होता है<br>माध्यक वर्ग \\(= \\boxed{180-190}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 180–190 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019e69ce-f74a-74e0-a197-9f7d34c846c3_EN.jpg?edu=639294371653349927","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019e69ce-f74a-74e0-a197-9f7d34c846c3_HI.jpg?edu=639294371776042170"]}},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000074152","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The following pie-chart represents the percentage-wise share of different forest types within a specified region. Analyze the data distribution provided in the chart and answer the question that follows.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019e6e29-944f-774a-802a-f8816ed10ef7_EN.jpg?edu=639294371653666367\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Let us assume that the 'Combined High Growth Zone' is made up of 'Tropical Evergreen' and 'Deciduous' forests, while the 'Sparse Zone' is made up of 'Scrub' and 'Mangrove' forests. By how many percentage points is the 'High Growth Zone' greater than the 'Sparse Zone'? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित पाई चार्ट किसी क्षेत्र में विभिन्न वन प्रकारों के प्रतिशत-वार हिस्से को दर्शाता है। चार्ट में दिए गए डेटा वितरण का विश्लेषण कीजिए और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019e6e29-944f-774a-802a-f8816ed10ef7_HI.jpg?edu=639294371776290787\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>मान लीजिए 'संयुक्त उच्च वृद्धि क्षेत्र' में 'उष्णकटिबंधीय सदाबहार' और 'पतझड़ी' वन आते हैं, जबकि 'विरल क्षेत्र' में 'झाड़ी' और 'मैंग्रोव' वन आते हैं। 'उच्च वृद्धि क्षेत्र', 'विरल क्षेत्र' से कितने प्रतिशत बिंदु अधिक है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"35"},"2":{"en":"40"},"3":{"en":"45"},"4":{"en":"50"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"High Growth Zone \\(= 30\\% + 35\\% = 65\\%\\)<br>Sparse Zone \\(= 10\\% + 10\\% = 20\\%\\)<br>Difference \\(= 65 - 20 = \\boxed{45}\\) percentage points<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 45.</b>","hi":"उच्च वृद्धि क्षेत्र \\(= 30\\% + 35\\% = 65\\%\\)<br>विरल क्षेत्र \\(= 10\\% + 10\\% = 20\\%\\)<br>अंतर \\(= 65 - 20 = \\boxed{45}\\) प्रतिशत बिंदु<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 45 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019e6e29-944f-774a-802a-f8816ed10ef7_EN.jpg?edu=639294371653666367","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019e6e29-944f-774a-802a-f8816ed10ef7_HI.jpg?edu=639294371776290787"]}},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000074153","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"An observer 1.5 m tall is 28.5 m away from a tower. The angle of elevation of the top of the tower from the observer's eye is 45°. What is the height of the tower? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"1.5 m लंबा एक प्रेक्षक मीनार से 28.5 m दूर है। प्रेक्षक की आँख से मीनार के शिखर का उन्नयन कोण 45° है। मीनार की ऊँचाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15 m"},"2":{"en":"20 m"},"3":{"en":"25 m"},"4":{"en":"30 m"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan 45° = \\frac{H - 1.5}{28.5} \\Rightarrow H - 1.5 = 28.5\\)<br>\\(H = 28.5 + 1.5\\)<br>\\(H = \\boxed{30\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 30 m.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan 45° = \\frac{H - 1.5}{28.5} \\Rightarrow H - 1.5 = 28.5\\)<br>\\(H = 28.5 + 1.5\\)<br>\\(H = \\boxed{30\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 30 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000074154","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"The average of 15 numbers is 72. The average of the first 8 numbers is 69, while the average of the last 6 numbers is 75. What is the ninth number? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"15 संख्याओं का औसत 72 है। पहली 8 संख्याओं का औसत 69 है, जबकि अंतिम 6 संख्याओं का औसत 75 है। नौवीं संख्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"66"},"2":{"en":"72"},"3":{"en":"78"},"4":{"en":"84"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Total \\(= 15 \\times 72 = 1080\\)<br>First 8 \\(= 8 \\times 69 = 552\\), last 6 \\(= 6 \\times 75 = 450\\)<br>Ninth \\(= 1080 - 552 - 450 = \\boxed{78}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 78.</b>","hi":"कुल \\(= 15 \\times 72 = 1080\\)<br>पहली 8 \\(= 8 \\times 69 = 552\\), अंतिम 6 \\(= 6 \\times 75 = 450\\)<br>नौवीं \\(= 1080 - 552 - 450 = \\boxed{78}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 78 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000074155","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"An E-Commerce platform tracks the number of attempts it takes to resolve customer disputes filed under a premium merchant category. The bar-graph below presents the distribution:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f88af-2151-70cb-a69a-111eb71f73aa_EN.jpg?edu=639294371654759845\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Find the absolute difference between the mode and the median of this distribution. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक ई-कॉमर्स प्लेटफ़ॉर्म ट्रैक करता है कि प्रीमियम व्यापारी श्रेणी में दर्ज ग्राहक विवादों को सुलझाने में कितने प्रयास लगते हैं। नीचे दिया गया बार-ग्राफ वितरण दर्शाता है:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f88af-2151-70cb-a69a-111eb71f73aa_HI.jpg?edu=639294371777090665\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>इस वितरण के बहुलक और माध्यक के बीच निरपेक्ष अंतर ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Frequencies: 14, 26, 35, 15, 7, 3 (total 100, even, so median is the mean of the 50th and 51st items)<br>Mode \\(= 3\\) attempts (highest frequency 35)<br>Cumulative: 14, 40, 75 … so both the 50th and 51st items fall in the '3' group → median \\(= 3\\)<br>Difference \\(= 3 - 3 = \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 0.</b>","hi":"आवृत्तियाँ: 14, 26, 35, 15, 7, 3 (कुल 100, सम, अतः माध्यक 50वें और 51वें मान का औसत है)<br>बहुलक \\(= 3\\) प्रयास (अधिकतम आवृत्ति 35)<br>संचयी: 14, 40, 75 … अतः 50वाँ और 51वाँ दोनों '3' समूह में हैं → माध्यक \\(= 3\\)<br>अंतर \\(= 3 - 3 = \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/EN/019f88af-2151-70cb-a69a-111eb71f73aa_EN.jpg?edu=639294371654759845","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct6/qimg/3/HI/019f88af-2151-70cb-a69a-111eb71f73aa_HI.jpg?edu=639294371777090665"]}}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000074156","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the wrongly spelt word out of the four alternatives. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Comprehention"},"2":{"en":"Surgeon"},"3":{"en":"Discovery"},"4":{"en":"Fathoms"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Comprehension (समझ) = the ability to understand something.</b><br><b>Comprehention</b> is wrong: “s” is missing before “-ion.”<br><b>Surgeon (शल्य चिकित्सक)</b> = a doctor who performs operations; spelling correct.<br><b>Discovery (खोज)</b> = the act of finding something; spelling correct.<br><b>Fathoms (फैदम)</b> = units for measuring water depth; spelling correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Comprehention.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000074157","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the wrongly spelt word out of the four alternatives. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Superstisious"},"2":{"en":"Courteously"},"3":{"en":"Superficial"},"4":{"en":"Fertilizer"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Superstitious (अंधविश्वासी) = believing in superstitions.</b><br><b>Superstisious</b> wrongly inserts “i” after “t”; the correct form is “superstitious.”<br><b>Courteously (विनम्रतापूर्वक)</b> = politely; spelling correct.<br><b>Superficial (सतही)</b> = existing on the surface or lacking depth; spelling correct.<br><b>Fertilizer (उर्वरक)</b> = a substance added to soil to aid plant growth; spelling correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Superstisious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000074158","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.<br>The witness was accused of being <u>mendacious</u> during the trial. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dishonest"},"2":{"en":"Truthful"},"3":{"en":"False"},"4":{"en":"Deceitful"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Mendacious (झूठा) = telling lies or being untruthful.</b><br><b>Dishonest (बेईमान)</b> = not honest<br><b>Truthful (सत्यवादी)</b> = telling the truth ✔<br><b>False (झूठा)</b> = not true<br><b>Deceitful (धोखेबाज)</b> = misleading others<br>More antonyms: honest, veracious, sincere.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Truthful.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000074159","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.<br>The witness gave a <u>murky</u> account of the incident, making it hard to follow. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dark"},"2":{"en":"Gloomy"},"3":{"en":"Obscure"},"4":{"en":"Clear"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Murky (धुंधला, अस्पष्ट) = dark, unclear or difficult to understand.</b><br><b>Dark (अंधेरा)</b> = lacking light<br><b>Gloomy (उदास)</b> = dark or depressing<br><b>Obscure (अस्पष्ट)</b> = not clearly expressed<br><b>Clear (स्पष्ट)</b> = easy to understand ✔<br>More antonyms: lucid, transparent, plain.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Clear.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000074160","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the correctly spelt word to replace the highlighted word in the given sentence.<br>Her <b>scintilating</b> wit charmed every single guest. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Scintilating"},"2":{"en":"Scintillating"},"3":{"en":"Scintallating"},"4":{"en":"Scintalating"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Scintillating (चमकीला, अत्यंत रोचक) = brilliantly lively or witty.</b><br>The correct spelling has double “l” and double “t”: “scin-til-lat-ing.”<br><b>Scintilating</b> lacks one “l”; <b>Scintallating</b> uses “a” instead of “i” after “scint”;<br><b>Scintalating</b> omits a “t” and an “l.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Scintillating.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000074161","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the correctly spelt word to replace the highlighted word in the given sentence.<br>A <b>propencity</b> for violence was noted during the investigation. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Propensity"},"2":{"en":"Propensitty"},"3":{"en":"Propencitty"},"4":{"en":"Propencity"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Propensity (प्रवृत्ति) = a natural tendency to behave in a particular way.</b><br>The correct spelling is “propensity,” with “-sity” at the end.<br><b>Propensitty</b> wrongly doubles “t”; <b>Propencitty</b> uses “c” and doubles “t”;<br><b>Propencity</b> wrongly uses “c” instead of “s.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Propensity.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000074162","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named P, Q, R, and S. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.<br>1. Economic growth is<br>P. the standard of living<br>Q. a sustained increase<br>R. in the production of<br>S. goods and services that improves<br>6. for the entire population. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRSP"},"2":{"en":"RSQP"},"3":{"en":"QPSR"},"4":{"en":"QSPR"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br>Q completes “Economic growth is a sustained increase.”<br>R and S continue the definition: “in the production of goods and services that improves.”<br>P joins the fixed ending: “the standard of living for the entire population.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000074163","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named P, Q, R, and S. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.<br>1. The concept of the Blue Economy<br>P. to promote economic growth<br>Q. while ensuring the environmental sustainability<br>R. seeks to harness ocean resources<br>S. and improved social inclusion<br>6. of the vast marine and coastal ecosystems. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PQSR"},"2":{"en":"RPSQ"},"3":{"en":"RSQP"},"4":{"en":"QSRP"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RPSQ</b><br>R gives the main verb phrase: “seeks to harness ocean resources.”<br>P adds the purpose “to promote economic growth,” and S adds “improved social inclusion.”<br>Q supplies the contrast “while ensuring environmental sustainability,” leading naturally into part 6.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): RPSQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000074164","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate option to fill the blank in the given sentence.<br>By the time the workshop ended yesterday, Rahul ___ the model that he ___ for three hours. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"had finished, had been building"},"2":{"en":"finished, was building"},"3":{"en":"has finished, is building"},"4":{"en":"finishes, built"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past perfect marks the earlier completed action; past perfect continuous marks its preceding duration.</b><br>“By the time … ended” places both actions before a past reference point.<br>Completed sentence: “Rahul <b>had finished</b> the model that he <b>had been building</b> for three hours.”<br>The other options use simple or present tenses that do not show this sequence and duration.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): had finished, had been building.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000074165","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate option to fill the blank in the given sentence.<br>If I ___ my camera battery last night, I ___ more photos during the walk today. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"charged, would take"},"2":{"en":"had charged, would have taken"},"3":{"en":"have charged, will take"},"4":{"en":"had charged, would take"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An unreal past condition uses “If + past perfect, … would have + past participle.”</b><br>The battery was not charged, and the opportunity for more photos was missed.<br>Completed sentence: “If I <b>had charged</b> my camera battery last night, I <b>would have taken</b> more photos during the walk today.”<br>Options 1 and 4 do not complete the hypothetical result; option 3 uses the wrong conditional pattern.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): had charged, would have taken.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000074166","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"From the given options, select the homonym that corresponds to both Definition (P) and Definition (Q).<br>(P) To adjust or compromise one's desires or actions to prevent conflict and cooperate harmoniously with others<br>(Q) To provide temporary lodging, physical space, or overnight living quarters for someone [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rehabilitate"},"2":{"en":"Accommodate"},"3":{"en":"Articulate"},"4":{"en":"Designate"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Accommodate (अनुकूल बनाना; ठहराने की व्यवस्था करना)</b><br>It means both to adapt to others’ needs and to provide lodging or sufficient space.<br><b>Rehabilitate (पुनर्वसित करना)</b> = restore to normal life<br><b>Articulate (स्पष्ट अभिव्यक्त करना)</b> = express clearly<br><b>Designate (नामित करना)</b> = appoint or specify officially<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Accommodate.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000074167","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Identify the option in which the underlined idiom has been used incorrectly.<br>A. The minister did not <u>mince words</u> during the live television broadcast, spending nearly forty minutes delivering vague, evasive responses.<br>B. When the journalist suggested that the CEO had intentionally misled investors, the executive angrily cut her off, accusing her of trying to <u>put words into his mouth</u>.<br>C. The eccentric philosophy professor loved to <u>talk in riddles</u>, frequently answering direct student questions with cryptic metaphors that left the entire lecture hall confused.<br>D. The interviewer accidentally <u>hit a raw nerve</u> when he asked the retired athlete about the career-ending knee injury that had cost his team the championship final. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The minister did not mince words during the live television broadcast, spending nearly forty minutes delivering vague, evasive responses."},"2":{"en":"When the journalist suggested that the CEO had intentionally misled investors, the executive angrily cut her off, accusing her of trying to put words into his mouth."},"3":{"en":"The eccentric philosophy professor loved to talk in riddles, frequently answering direct student questions with cryptic metaphors that left the entire lecture hall confused."},"4":{"en":"The interviewer accidentally hit a raw nerve when he asked the retired athlete about the career-ending knee injury that had cost his team the championship final."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Mince words (शब्दों को घुमा-फिराकर कहना) = speak indirectly or euphemistically.</b><br>“Did not mince words” means spoke bluntly, which contradicts “vague, evasive responses”; hence A is incorrect.<br>“Put words into his mouth” fits falsely attributing a statement.<br>“Talk in riddles” fits cryptic replies; “hit a raw nerve” fits touching a painful subject.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The minister did not mince words during the live television broadcast, spending nearly forty minutes delivering vague, evasive responses..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000074168","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Read the sentences provided in options A, B, C, and D carefully. While three of the sentences are grammatically sound, one contains an “article usage” error. Identify the option with the error.<br>A. A research team at the University of Cambridge successfully engineered a stable topological qubit, outpacing rival physics departments across Europe.<br>B. Excavations funded by Yale University unearthed a beautifully preserved fossilised apex predator in the badlands of Montana.<br>C. While the Administrator refused to comment on the launch failure, Director General Faiz issued a comprehensive technical briefing to the press.<br>D. The diplomatic delegation travelled from Netherlands to the Czech Republic to ratify the new maritime trade agreement. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A research team at the University of Cambridge successfully engineered a stable topological qubit, outpacing rival physics departments across Europe."},"2":{"en":"Excavations funded by Yale University unearthed a beautifully preserved fossilised apex predator in the badlands of Montana."},"3":{"en":"While the Administrator refused to comment on the launch failure, Director General Faiz issued a comprehensive technical briefing to the press."},"4":{"en":"The diplomatic delegation travelled from Netherlands to the Czech Republic to ratify the new maritime trade agreement."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The definite article “the” is used with “Netherlands.”</b><br>Option D should read “travelled from <b>the Netherlands</b> to the Czech Republic.”<br>“The University of Cambridge” is correctly used in A.<br>No article is required before “Yale University” or “Montana” in B; C uses its articles and titles appropriately.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The diplomatic delegation travelled from Netherlands to the Czech Republic to ratify the new maritime trade agreement..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000074169","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Read the sentences below carefully and identify which one contains a grammatical or structural error.<br>(P) The agricultural collective harvested as many more metric tons of organic grain than the commercial farming conglomerate during the fiscal year.<br>(Q) The more thoroughly the research cohort analysed the genomic sequencing data, the fewer anomalies they found in the control group. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only P"},"2":{"en":"Only Q"},"3":{"en":"Both P and Q"},"4":{"en":"Neither P nor Q"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Equality uses “as + adjective + as,” not “as … than.”</b><br>P mixes two comparative structures. Use either “as many metric tons … as” or “more metric tons … than.”<br>Q correctly uses the paired comparative structure “The more thoroughly …, the fewer ….”<br>Therefore, only P is erroneous.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only P.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000074170","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Read the passive statement. If you were to explain the action in a single, direct sentence, which of the following active voice options would be the most accurate translation?<br>The narrative's deeply cynical conclusion is created by the suggestion that rescue is ultimately brought about by appalling savagery, whereas it fails to be achieved by coordinated and purposeful efforts. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The suggestion that appalling savagery ultimately bring about rescue, whereas coordinated and purposeful efforts fail to achieve it, creates the narrative's deeply cynical conclusion."},"2":{"en":"The suggestion that appalling savagery ultimately bring about rescue, whereas coordinate and purposeful efforts fail to achieve it, creates the narrative's deeply cynical conclusion."},"3":{"en":"The suggestion that appalling savagery ultimately brings about rescue, whereas coordinated and purposeful efforts fail to achieve it, creates the narrative's deep cynical conclusion."},"4":{"en":"The suggestion that appalling savagery ultimately brings about rescue, whereas coordinated and purposeful efforts fail to achieve it, creates the narrative's deeply cynical conclusion."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The agent “the suggestion” becomes the subject of the active verb “creates.”</b><br>The singular noun “savagery” requires “brings about,” and the adjective “coordinated” and adverb “deeply” must remain unchanged.<br>Options 1 and 2 use the uninflected “bring”; option 2 also uses “coordinate.”<br>Option 3 wrongly changes “deeply” to “deep.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The suggestion that appalling savagery ultimately brings about rescue, whereas coordinated and purposeful efforts fail to achieve it, creates the narrative's deeply cynical conclusion..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000074171","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Convert the following sentence from direct to indirect speech. Choose the option that best represents the correct transformation.<br>Janvi said to Kamal, “I travel about in an old utility vehicle, which is a simple transport setup with basic bedding on its floor, stopping where people gather to listen and observe; however, in the process, I have formed an impression of my surroundings, the accuracy of which is limited only by my own shortcomings.” [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Janvi told Kamal that she travelled about in an old utility vehicle, which was a simple transport setup with basic bedding on it's floor, stopping where people gathered to listen and observe; however, in the process, she had formed an impression of her surroundings, the accuracy of which was limited only by her own shortcomings."},"2":{"en":"Janvi told Kamal that she travelled about in an old utility vehicle, which was a simple transport setup with basic bedding on its floor, stopping where people gathered to listen and observe; however, in the process, she had formed an impression of her surroundings, the accuracy of which was limited only by her own shortcomings."},"3":{"en":"Janvi told Kamal that she travelled about in an old utility vehicle, which was a simple transport setup with basic bedding on it's floor, stopping where people gather to listen and observe; however, in the process, she had formed an impression of her surroundings, the accuracy of which was limited only by her own shortcomings."},"4":{"en":"Janvi told Kamal that she travelled about in an old utility vehicle, which was a simple transport setup with basic bedding on its floor, stopping where people gathered to listen and observed; however, in the process, she had formed an impression of her surroundings, the accuracy of which is limited only by her own shortcomings."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Backshift present tenses and change first-person pronouns to third person.</b><br>“Travel” becomes “travelled,” “gather” becomes “gathered,” and “have formed” becomes “had formed.”<br>The possessive form is “its,” without an apostrophe.<br>Options 1 and 3 wrongly use “it’s”; option 3 also retains “gather,” while option 4 uses “observed” and fails to backshift “is.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Janvi told Kamal that she travelled about in an old utility vehicle, which was a simple transport setup with basic bedding on its floor, stopping where people gathered to listen and observe; however, in the process, she had formed an impression of her surroundings, the accuracy of which was limited only by her own shortcomings..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000074172","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Read the sentence below carefully. Choose the option (A/B/C) that best improves the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select Option D (No improvement required).<br>It was the clinical analyst's conclusion that the patient's underlying trauma was driven by a deep, unresolved desire, desires which continuously sabotaged their interpersonal relationships. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The clinical analyst concluded that underlying trauma of the patient being driven by a deep, unresolved desire, the desire that continuously sabotaged their interpersonal relationships."},"2":{"en":"The clinical analyst concluded that the patient's underlying trauma was driven by a deep, unresolved desire, a desire that continuously sabotaged their interpersonal relationships."},"3":{"en":"It was concluded by the clinical analyst that a deep, unresolved desire was driven the patient's underlying trauma, and their interpersonal relationships were continuously sabotaged by that desire."},"4":{"en":"No improvement required"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Use a clear finite clause and a singular appositive to avoid a mismatched plural noun.</b><br>Option B supplies “The clinical analyst concluded” and correctly repeats “a desire” before the relative clause.<br>A uses the non-finite “being driven” and an awkward possessive structure.<br>C reverses the logical relationship; D retains the mismatch “a … desire, desires which.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The clinical analyst concluded that the patient's underlying trauma was driven by a deep, unresolved desire, a desire that continuously sabotaged their interpersonal relationships..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000074173","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Read the sentence below carefully. Choose the option (A/B/C) that best improves the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select Option D (No improvement required).<br>The constitutional jurist argued that by altering the founding charter without a public referendum would nullify it and render it completely void, an act of total and absolute betrayal of the social contract. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The constitutional jurist argued that altering the founding charter without a public referendum would render it null and void, representing a total betrayal of the social contract."},"2":{"en":"The constitutional jurist argued that any alteration in the founding charter without holding a public referendum would null it as completely void, being a total betrayal of the social contract."},"3":{"en":"The constitutional jurist argued that in altering the founding charter without a public referendum, we would void it totally, acting as an absolute betrayal of the social contract."},"4":{"en":"No improvement required"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A gerund phrase can be the subject; “null and void” is the standard concise legal expression.</b><br>Option A removes the unnecessary “by” and redundancies such as “completely void” and “total and absolute.”<br>B incorrectly uses “null” as a verb and remains redundant.<br>C introduces an unsupported “we” and an awkward participial ending; D retains the original structural error.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The constitutional jurist argued that altering the founding charter without a public referendum would render it null and void, representing a total betrayal of the social contract..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000074174","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Select the correct passive form of the given sentence.<br>The judge will deliver the final verdict in the court tomorrow. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The final verdict will have been delivered in the court by the judge tomorrow."},"2":{"en":"The final verdict will be delivered in the court by the judge tomorrow."},"3":{"en":"The final verdict would be delivered in the court by the judge tomorrow."},"4":{"en":"The final verdict is delivered in the court by the judge tomorrow."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Future simple passive = will be + past participle.</b><br>“The final verdict” becomes the subject and “the judge” becomes the agent.<br>Correct form: “The final verdict <b>will be delivered</b> in the court by the judge tomorrow.”<br>Option 1 changes the aspect, option 3 changes “will” to “would,” and option 4 uses present passive.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The final verdict will be delivered in the court by the judge tomorrow..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000074175","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"The following sentence is given in Indirect Speech. Select the option that correctly expresses it in Direct Speech.<br>Tertius Lydgate questioned himself wretchedly why he had allowed the shallow material desires of Rosamond Vincy to ruin his scientific ambitions. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tertius Lydgate questioned himself wretchedly, “Why did I allow the shallow material desires of Rosamond Vincy to ruin my scientific ambitions?”"},"2":{"en":"Tertius Lydgate questioned himself, “wretchedly why he had allowed the shallow material desires of Rosamond Vincy to ruin his scientific ambitions.”"},"3":{"en":"Tertius Lydgate questions himself wretchedly, “Why did I allowed the shallow material desires of Rosamond Vincy to ruined my scientific ambitions?”"},"4":{"en":"Tertius Lydgate questioned himself wretchedly. “Why I had allowed the shallow material desires of Rosamond Vincy to ruin my scientific ambitions?”"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Restore the direct question with “did + base verb” and first-person pronouns.</b><br>“He had allowed” becomes “Why did I allow,” and “his” becomes “my.”<br>B retains indirect third-person wording and misplaces “wretchedly.”<br>C has “did I allowed” and “to ruined”; D lacks the auxiliary “did” required in the direct question.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Tertius Lydgate questioned himself wretchedly, “Why did I allow the shallow material desires of Rosamond Vincy to ruin my scientific ambitions?”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000074176","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words or phrases from the options given below.<br><br>Urban farming has emerged as a practical response to growing concerns about food security, environmental degradation, and rapid urbanisation. Once regarded as a marginal activity, it is now increasingly recognised as a sustainable means of supplementing food supplies while promoting ecological awareness. (A) many city dwellers have transformed vacant rooftops, balconies, and community spaces into productive gardens that contribute to local biodiversity. These initiatives not only reduce dependence on long-distance transportation but also foster a stronger sense of community responsibility. (B) urban farming cannot entirely replace conventional agriculture, it serves as a valuable complement by encouraging responsible consumption and minimising food waste. In addition to producing fresh vegetables, urban gardens often (C) social barriers by bringing together people from diverse economic and cultural backgrounds. Such interactions encourage cooperation and the exchange of practical knowledge, thereby strengthening neighbourhood ties. Moreover, the movement has generated widespread interest among policymakers and environmentalists, who regard it as an effective means of enhancing urban (D) ___. As cities continue to expand, the integration of green spaces into residential areas is increasingly viewed as a necessity rather than a luxury.<br><br>Consequently, the long-term success of urban farming depends not only on individual enthusiasm but also (E) supportive public policies, technological innovation, and sustained community participation. If managed effectively, urban farming may become an indispensable element of future city planning, helping to balance economic development with environmental responsibility.<br><br><br>Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank (A). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Encouraged by growing environmental awareness"},"2":{"en":"Encourage growing environmental awareness"},"3":{"en":"Having encourage environmental awareness"},"4":{"en":"Environmental awareness encouraging"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A past participial phrase correctly modifies “many city dwellers.”</b><br>They are <b>encouraged by</b> growing environmental awareness, so the passive participle is logical.<br>“Encourage” is a bare verb and cannot open this modifier; “having encourage” is ungrammatical.<br>“Environmental awareness encouraging” leaves the clause incomplete.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Encouraged by growing environmental awareness.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000074177","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words or phrases from the options given below.<br><br>Urban farming has emerged as a practical response to growing concerns about food security, environmental degradation, and rapid urbanisation. Once regarded as a marginal activity, it is now increasingly recognised as a sustainable means of supplementing food supplies while promoting ecological awareness. (A) many city dwellers have transformed vacant rooftops, balconies, and community spaces into productive gardens that contribute to local biodiversity. These initiatives not only reduce dependence on long-distance transportation but also foster a stronger sense of community responsibility. (B) urban farming cannot entirely replace conventional agriculture, it serves as a valuable complement by encouraging responsible consumption and minimising food waste. In addition to producing fresh vegetables, urban gardens often (C) social barriers by bringing together people from diverse economic and cultural backgrounds. Such interactions encourage cooperation and the exchange of practical knowledge, thereby strengthening neighbourhood ties. Moreover, the movement has generated widespread interest among policymakers and environmentalists, who regard it as an effective means of enhancing urban (D) ___. As cities continue to expand, the integration of green spaces into residential areas is increasingly viewed as a necessity rather than a luxury.<br><br>Consequently, the long-term success of urban farming depends not only on individual enthusiasm but also (E) supportive public policies, technological innovation, and sustained community participation. If managed effectively, urban farming may become an indispensable element of future city planning, helping to balance economic development with environmental responsibility.<br><br><br>Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank (B). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Unless"},"2":{"en":"Therefore"},"3":{"en":"Although"},"4":{"en":"Likewise"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Although (यद्यपि) introduces a contrast.</b><br>The passage contrasts urban farming’s inability to replace conventional agriculture with its value as a complement.<br>“Unless” expresses a condition; “therefore” expresses a result; “likewise” adds similarity.<br>Only “although” fits both the grammar and meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Although.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000074178","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words or phrases from the options given below.<br><br>Urban farming has emerged as a practical response to growing concerns about food security, environmental degradation, and rapid urbanisation. Once regarded as a marginal activity, it is now increasingly recognised as a sustainable means of supplementing food supplies while promoting ecological awareness. (A) many city dwellers have transformed vacant rooftops, balconies, and community spaces into productive gardens that contribute to local biodiversity. These initiatives not only reduce dependence on long-distance transportation but also foster a stronger sense of community responsibility. (B) urban farming cannot entirely replace conventional agriculture, it serves as a valuable complement by encouraging responsible consumption and minimising food waste. In addition to producing fresh vegetables, urban gardens often (C) social barriers by bringing together people from diverse economic and cultural backgrounds. Such interactions encourage cooperation and the exchange of practical knowledge, thereby strengthening neighbourhood ties. Moreover, the movement has generated widespread interest among policymakers and environmentalists, who regard it as an effective means of enhancing urban (D) ___. As cities continue to expand, the integration of green spaces into residential areas is increasingly viewed as a necessity rather than a luxury.<br><br>Consequently, the long-term success of urban farming depends not only on individual enthusiasm but also (E) supportive public policies, technological innovation, and sustained community participation. If managed effectively, urban farming may become an indispensable element of future city planning, helping to balance economic development with environmental responsibility.<br><br><br>Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank (C). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"bring over"},"2":{"en":"break down"},"3":{"en":"call off"},"4":{"en":"put aside"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Break down barriers (बाधाओं को दूर करना) = remove obstacles or divisions.</b><br>Urban gardens remove social barriers by connecting people from diverse backgrounds.<br><b>Bring over (साथ लाना)</b> = bring someone or something to a place<br><b>Call off (रद्द करना)</b> = cancel; <b>put aside (अलग रखना)</b> = reserve or disregard<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): break down.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000074179","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words or phrases from the options given below.<br><br>Urban farming has emerged as a practical response to growing concerns about food security, environmental degradation, and rapid urbanisation. Once regarded as a marginal activity, it is now increasingly recognised as a sustainable means of supplementing food supplies while promoting ecological awareness. (A) many city dwellers have transformed vacant rooftops, balconies, and community spaces into productive gardens that contribute to local biodiversity. These initiatives not only reduce dependence on long-distance transportation but also foster a stronger sense of community responsibility. (B) urban farming cannot entirely replace conventional agriculture, it serves as a valuable complement by encouraging responsible consumption and minimising food waste. In addition to producing fresh vegetables, urban gardens often (C) social barriers by bringing together people from diverse economic and cultural backgrounds. Such interactions encourage cooperation and the exchange of practical knowledge, thereby strengthening neighbourhood ties. Moreover, the movement has generated widespread interest among policymakers and environmentalists, who regard it as an effective means of enhancing urban (D) ___. As cities continue to expand, the integration of green spaces into residential areas is increasingly viewed as a necessity rather than a luxury.<br><br>Consequently, the long-term success of urban farming depends not only on individual enthusiasm but also (E) supportive public policies, technological innovation, and sustained community participation. If managed effectively, urban farming may become an indispensable element of future city planning, helping to balance economic development with environmental responsibility.<br><br><br>Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank (D). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"resilience"},"2":{"en":"hesitation"},"3":{"en":"extravagance"},"4":{"en":"fragility"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Resilience (लचीलापन, संकट से उबरने की क्षमता) = the ability to withstand or recover from difficulties.</b><br>Green spaces and urban farming enhance a city’s resilience.<br><b>Hesitation (हिचकिचाहट)</b> = reluctance<br><b>Extravagance (फिजूलखर्ची)</b> = wasteful spending<br><b>Fragility (नाजुकता)</b> = weakness or vulnerability, the opposite of the intended idea<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): resilience.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000074180","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words or phrases from the options given below.<br><br>Urban farming has emerged as a practical response to growing concerns about food security, environmental degradation, and rapid urbanisation. Once regarded as a marginal activity, it is now increasingly recognised as a sustainable means of supplementing food supplies while promoting ecological awareness. (A) many city dwellers have transformed vacant rooftops, balconies, and community spaces into productive gardens that contribute to local biodiversity. These initiatives not only reduce dependence on long-distance transportation but also foster a stronger sense of community responsibility. (B) urban farming cannot entirely replace conventional agriculture, it serves as a valuable complement by encouraging responsible consumption and minimising food waste. In addition to producing fresh vegetables, urban gardens often (C) social barriers by bringing together people from diverse economic and cultural backgrounds. Such interactions encourage cooperation and the exchange of practical knowledge, thereby strengthening neighbourhood ties. Moreover, the movement has generated widespread interest among policymakers and environmentalists, who regard it as an effective means of enhancing urban (D) ___. As cities continue to expand, the integration of green spaces into residential areas is increasingly viewed as a necessity rather than a luxury.<br><br>Consequently, the long-term success of urban farming depends not only on individual enthusiasm but also (E) supportive public policies, technological innovation, and sustained community participation. If managed effectively, urban farming may become an indispensable element of future city planning, helping to balance economic development with environmental responsibility.<br><br><br>Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank (E). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"on"},"2":{"en":"regarding"},"3":{"en":"at"},"4":{"en":"toward"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Depend on” is the fixed prepositional verb meaning to rely on something.</b><br>The sentence says success depends not only on enthusiasm but also <b>on</b> supportive policies and participation.<br>“Regarding” means concerning; “at” and “toward” do not complete “depends” idiomatically.<br>Parallel “not only … but also” also supports repeating “on.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): on.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};